PVD("rwanda_ndp_2017-2024",{"docs":["","ndp_2017 2024_nst1"],"s":{"1":[[1,"24","6","Multi-Hazard Early Warning Systems Strengthening","These will include strengthening multi- hazard early warning systems,",""],[1,"24","6","Rapid Disaster Response Capacity Strengthening","strengthening capacity for rapid response and management of disasters,",""],[1,"24","6","Catchment Restoration and Watershed Management","restoring catchment areas, improving watershed management, and implementing flood control measures in high-risk areas, such as the Northern and Western Provinces in partnership with local communities.",""],[1,"33","6","Disaster Preparedness, Response and Mitigation Mechanisms","Continue to improve mechanisms for disaster preparedness response and mitigation in different sectors with priority to big sectors such as; agriculture, infrastructure, education, urbanization, ICT, health, environment and natural resources.",""],[1,"34","5","Mainstreamed Disaster Risk Reduction and Response Across Sectors","Mainstreaming disaster management in Rwanda involves integrating Disaster Risk Reduction (DRR) and response efforts across various sectors to effectively mitigate, prepare for, respond to, and recover from disasters.",""],[1,"34","5","Sector Disaster Risk Mitigation Plans","Emphasis will be put on sustaining progress and strengthening gender-responsive capacities for disaster risk reduction and management and enhancing resilience through developing and implementing sector disaster risk mitigation plans, promoting integrated and inclusive approaches focusing on the most vulnerable to risk management such as; joint inspections to ensure compliance, strengthening and implementing community-based disaster resilience measures including putting in place water harvesting and drainage systems and house retrofitting.",""],[1,"44","3","Weather Forecasting and Early Warning Systems Strengthening","Strengthening capacities for weather forecasting and early warning systems to increase reliability and accuracy of information for informed decision making;",""],[1,"44","5","Disaster Management Plans and Tools Implementation","Continuing implementation of the disaster management plans and tools including district disaster management plans and other contingency plans.",""],[1,"73","3","Disaster Preparedness, Response, and Mitigation Mechanisms","Continue to improve mechanisms for disaster preparedness response and mitigation in different sectors",""],[1,"77","3","Disaster Rapid Response and Management Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen capacity for rapid response and management of disasters (including district emergency command posts)",""]],"2":[[1,"36","6","Cross-Sectoral Policy Alignment with NST-2 Priorities","Ensure cross-sectoral alignment of policies with NST-2 priorities",""],[1,"36","7","Cross-Sectoral Coordination for NST-2 Execution","Ensure cross-sectoral coordination for the execution of NST-2 priorities",""],[1,"38","6","Development Partner Funding Alignment to NST2 Priorities","Ensure alignment of development partners' funding and resources to NST2 priorities",""],[1,"38","10","Ministerial Consultation and Engagement Platform for NST2","Serve as a Ministerial platform for consultation and :selected: engagement on policies and strategies relating to the NST2",""],[1,"40","3","Sector-Level Prioritization and Resource Allocation Support","Provide input to prioritization and resource :selected: allocation at sector level in line with NST2 priorities",""],[1,"41","3","District Partner Coordination and Mobilization for DDS Implementation","Coordinate and mobilize partners in the district :selected: including, the private sector, civil society and other stakeholders to ensure successful implementation of DDS aligned to NST2",""],[1,"41","6","National Planning and Investment Coordination","Coordinate national planning, investments, :selected: monitoring, resource mobilization, prioritization and allocation in line with NST2 priorities",""],[1,"42","1","Development Partner Coordination and Alignment Mechanism","Coordinate development partners and ensure :selected: alignment of interventions and resources to NST2 priorities",""],[1,"42","6","Coordination of District Development Strategy Elaboration","Coordinate the process for elaboration of Cok/ District Development Strategies in collaboration with Cok, Provinces and Districts",""],[1,"42","10","District-Level Stakeholder Coordination and Engagement Forums","Support strengthening of stakeholder coordination and engagement forums at the district level",""],[1,"42","12","District Monitoring and Evaluation System Strengthening","Support development and strengthening of robust monitoring and evaluation systems in Districts to support tracking of performance and lesson learning in implementation",""],[1,"42","13","Local Government Resource Mobilization Support","Support resource mobilization for local :selected: governments aligned to CoK/DDS and NST2 priorities",""],[1,"43","6","Institutional Framework and Coordination Strengthening","institutional frameworks, planning and coordination structures will be optimized and aligned with NST2 priorities.",""],[1,"43","6","Cross-Sectoral Coordination Strengthening","This includes strengthening cross-sectoral coordination, improving project design, and strengthening collaboration and engagement at all levels.",""],[1,"43","8","Private Sector Engagement Scale-Up","the engagement of the :selected: private sector will be scaled up across sectors, most especially in job creation, exports, industry, investment, and tourism among others",""],[1,"43","8","Bankable Investment Project Development Support","The private sector will also be engaged in developing bankable investment projects that support the delivery of NST2 priorities",""],[1,"44","2","Procurement Process Improvement and Joint Monitoring Mechanism","procurement processes and enhance regular joint monitoring and feedback processes to fast-track and unlock financing for major projects and programs.",""],[1,"44","2","Capacity Strengthening for Implementing Agencies and Districts","Lastly, the capabilities of implementing agencies and districts will be reinforced to deliver programs, projects and services effectively.",""],[1,"44","4","Integrated Government Planning Strengthening","Integrated planning: planning functions will be strengthened across government, particularly for key issues such as job creation, exports and manufacturing, stunting, private sector development, and poverty reduction.",""],[1,"44","5","Integrated Economic and Spatial Planning","Economic and spatial planning will be further integrated to ensure efficient resource allocation in accordance with designated land uses, maximizing the development impact of projects and programs on citizens.",""],[1,"50","3","Implementation and Delivery Strengthening Mechanism","Strengthening mechanisms for implementation and delivery.",""]],"3":[[1,"21","10","National Single Digital ID Rollout","A Single Digital ID will be rolled out nationally to improve the quality and efficiency of public service delivery through a trusted, secure and resilient digital ecosystem.",""],[1,"21","10","Government Service Digitization Programme","All government services will be fully digitized",""],[1,"21","10","Data-Driven Public Sector Decision-Making Initiative","This will involve integrating innovation, digital, and emerging technologies (AI, advanced robotics, etc.) to facilitate data-driven decision-making in key sectors such as education, health, agriculture, industry, government performance management, judiciary, finance, and the private sector among others.",""],[1,"38","3","Government Online Service Delivery Expansion","Ensure 100% Government services are delivered online by 2024 from 40% in 2017.",""],[1,"44","3","Technology- and Data-Driven NST2 Implementation System","The systems supporting NST2 implementation will rely on technology, data, and evidence-based decision-making.",""],[1,"76","2","E-Government Service Delivery Expansion","Ensure all Government services are delivered online by 2024",""]],"4":[[1,"20","6","Skills and Local Capacity Development Support","Academy will support the creation of the necessary skills and local capacity to sustain the growth of the sector.",""],[1,"32","12","PFM Skills Development Pipeline","A sustainable pipeline of critical PFM skills will be developed to support these objectives.",""],[1,"32","12","PFM Learning and Development Strategy Update","This will be achieved by updating learning and development strategies to prioritize essential PFM competencies and increasing the capacity to implement advanced PFM practices at decentralized levels through professional bodies.",""],[1,"34","5","Public Institution Capacity and Service Delivery Strengthening","Strengthen capable and responsible public institutions committed to citizens' advancement and efficient service delivery,",""],[1,"37","6","Mainstream Governance for Production Across Sectors","Mainstream governance for production across sectors and enhance capacities of public institutions and performance.",""],[1,"40","3","National Capacity Development Policy, Strategy and Implementation Plan","The National Capacity Development Policy, Strategy and Implementation Plan approved by Cabinet in 2016 will provide the framework and act as the main reference for guiding capacity development interventions.",""],[1,"41","1","Annual Capacity Development Planning","gaps and preparation of annual capacity development plans with strategies required for enhanced delivery.",""],[1,"41","1","Institutional Coordination and Training Standards","Emphasis will be put in appropriate coordination at the institutional level through setting standards in providing trainings, promoting innovation and learning, and using the RBM policy framework for monitoring and evaluation.",""],[1,"76","2","Governance Mainstreaming and Public Institution Capacity Strengthening","Mainstream governance for production across different sectors and enhance capacities of public institutions and performance",""],[1,"77","3","Corporate Governance Strengthening in Cooperatives and Community Development Initiatives","Enhance corporate governance, particularly within cooperatives and community development initiatives",""]],"5":[[1,"30","2","Public Health Emergency Surveillance and Early Warning Systems","Key initiatives include developing, reinforcing and rolling out robust event monitoring and early warning systems",""],[1,"30","2","Emergency Health Response Infrastructure and Services","establishing and improving the quality of emergency health response infrastructure and services",""],[1,"30","2","Health Security Collaboration and Partnership Strengthening","strengthening multisectoral collaboration and international partnerships in health security",""]],"6":[[1,"28","7","Health Infrastructure and Workforce Strengthening","Quality health care will be enhanced through providing adequate health infrastructure, skilled and motivated health workforce as well as enabling health systems.",""],[1,"29","1","Health Infrastructure Expansion and Facility Equipment","Continuing to expand health infrastructure and equip health facilities",""],[1,"29","1","Health Facility Construction and Upgrading Programme","Construct and upgrade health facilities with adequate equipment.",""],[1,"29","2","Maternal Mortality Reduction and Child Health Improvement Programme","Specific interventions will include maintaining high vaccination coverage and delivery at health facilities above 90%.",""],[1,"29","3","Health Workforce Expansion and Retention Strategy","Increase the number and capacity of human resources for health including: general practitioners, specialists, nurses, midwives and qualified administrators",""],[1,"30","1","Community NCD Prevention and Screening Services","This will be achieved through undertaking community mobilization to prevent diseases through maintaining hygiene, promoting physical exercises for all age groups, regular health checkups and scaling up screening services in communities and health facilities.",""],[1,"30","1","Universal Access to TB, Malaria, and HIV Treatment","Furthermore, this will be reinforced by sustaining the universal access to TB, Malaria, HIV treatment for all, ensuring availability, accessibility and affordability of quality care and treatment for NCD patients.",""],[1,"30","2","Health Infrastructure Modernization and Facility Equipping","There will be a focus on modernizing health infrastructure and fully equipping health facilities to ensure high-quality healthcare.",""],[1,"30","3","Medical Tourism and Health Infrastructure Expansion","Rwanda will be positioned as a medical tourism hub by developing critical investments in health infrastructure and systems in partnership with the private sector.",""],[1,"30","3","Expansion of Specialized Health Facilities and Services","This includes expanding health facilities and services in the Kigali Health City and other areas of the country to offer specialized health care.",""],[1,"41","3","Integrated HIV Prevention and Treatment Package","Rwanda has made extensive gains in the prevention and management of Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV) using an integrated package of components such as Voluntary counselling and testing (VCT), Prevention of mother-to-child Transmission (PMTCT), male circumcision, Behavior Change Communication (BCC), HIV treatment, and the recently introduced test and treat program for scaling-up prevention and treatment.",""],[1,"41","4","Self-Testing and Behavior Change Promotion","promoting self-testing methods, increasing awareness and promoting behavior change.",""],[1,"41","6","Mass Sports, Early Screening, and Behavior Change for Prevention","Rwanda's strategy will focus on 3 aspects: i) prevention through promoting mass sports for all, early screening, behavior change with regards to risk factors and",""],[1,"71","8","Health Facility Construction, Upgrading and Equipment","Construct/upgrade and equip Health facilities",""],[1,"71","8","Maternal and Child Health Improvement Measures","Improve Maternal Mortality and Child Health through maintaining high vaccination coverage and delivery at health facilities",""],[1,"71","8","Health Workforce Planning and Retention Strategy","Improve the coordination of health workforce production based on the actual and projected needs as well as establish retention strategies for the skilled workforce",""]],"7":[[1,"28","3","Malnutrition Prevention and Management Strategy","Implement both prevention and management strategies to eradicate all forms of malnutrition.",""],[1,"28","4","Strengthen Multi-sectoral Nutrition Coordination","Strengthening Multi-sectoral coordination through the Nutrition Secretariat and strengthen the social cluster coordination at decentralized levels up to the village.",""],[1,"28","5","Food and Nutrition Supplement Distribution","Distributing Food and vitamin supplements using Fortified Blended Food (FBF), and one Cup of milk per child, to those already affected.",""],[1,"28","6","Village-Level Nutrition and Antenatal Care Promotion","Promoting at the village level the 1,000 days of good nutrition and antenatal care.",""],[1,"42","1","Healthy Nutrition Promotion","healthy nutrition.",""],[1,"71","5","Multi-sectoral Nutrition Coordination Strengthening","Strengthen Multi-sectoral coordination through the Nutrition Secretariat",""],[1,"71","5","Decentralized Social Cluster Nutrition Coordination","Strengthen the social cluster coordination at decentralized levels up to the village.",""],[1,"71","5","Targeted Food and Vitamin Supplement Distribution","Distribute Food and vitamin supplements using Fortified Blended Food (FBF), one Cup of milk per child, to those already affected.",""],[1,"71","5","Village Nutrition and Antenatal Care Sensitization","Promote at the village level the 1,000 days of good nutrition and antenatal care through sensitizing households on good nutrition and hygiene practices at household and community level.",""]],"8":[[1,"11","1","Kigali Special Economic Zone Development","a fully developed special economic zone in Kigali",""],[1,"12","5","Industrialization and Export Base Upgrading","Promote industrialization and attain a structural shift in the export base to high-value goods and services with the aim of growing exports by 17% annu- ally.",""],[1,"12","6","Strengthening the Made in Rwanda Policy","The implementation of the \"Made in Rwanda\" policy and related interventions will be strengthened to ensure production of a high proportion of essential and high-value items locally, grow exports and reduce imports.",""],[1,"17","4","Industrial Development, Export Promotion and Trade Infrastructure Expansion","Promote industrial development, export promotion and expansion of trade related infrastructure",""],[1,"17","10","Manufacturing and Production Scale-Up for Essential and High-Value Products","Scaling up manufacturing and production of essential and high-value products to satisfy the local market demand and reduce dependence on imports",""],[1,"17","10","Priority Sub-Sector Development and Support Programme","Develop and support priority sub-sectors with high potential for growth and employment including: Agro-processing, Construction, Light manufacturing, Meat and Dairy, Leather, Textiles and Garments, Horticulture, Tourism, Knowledge based services, Value addition and processing of Mining products, Creative Arts, Aviation, Logistics, and Transportation.",""],[1,"19","8","Made in Rwanda Brand Promotion Initiative","Continue to promote the 'Made in Rwanda' brand working with the private sector to recapture at least USD 400 Millions of imports by 2024.",""],[1,"19","9","Local Manufacturing Industry Expansion","Establish and expand industries working with the private sector to promote locally produced materials and \"Made in Rwanda\" including: a pharmaceutical plant, a mosquito nets manufacturing plant, a chemical fertilizer plant, Industries for the production of construction materials such as ceramics, steel & Iron, cement and a packaging materials plant.",""],[1,"21","12","Industrial Parks Development and Kigali Special Economic Zone Expansion","Construct and develop industrial parks in provinces and expand the Kigali Special Economic Zone with capacity of 350 companies operating therein by 2024.",""],[1,"22","4","Mineral Processing and Value Addition Investment Promotion","The private sector will be attracted to invest in mineral processing and value addition.",""],[1,"22","5","Coffee Value Addition Upgrading","Value addition upgrading will be a key component of agricultural export growth.",""],[1,"22","5","Tea Processing Factory Expansion","Tea processing factories will be increased in numbers and in capacity (from 15 to 19 factories).",""],[1,"22","5","Agro-Processing Raw Material Access Support","Agro processing industries will be facilitated to access raw materials working with farmers and the private sector through improving the framework of contract farming and setting up of industrial blocs among others.",""],[1,"48","2","Value-Added Production and Trade Connectivity Initiatives","Sustained higher economic growth will involve orienting the economy towards higher value added activities and the production of tradeable, requiring investment, scale, innovation and the strengthening of regional and global trade connections.",""],[1,"50","2","Private Investment Expansion","the NST1 envisages significant increases in private investment, which will rise from 14.4% of GDP in 2017 to 21.2% by 2024.",""],[1,"51","2","Mining Sector Modernization and Expansion","the mining sector is projected to achieve 23.0% average growth per year from 2017 to 2024 with plans to modernize and expand the sector",""],[1,"51","2","Industrial Parks Completion for Agro-Processing and Textiles Growth","Furthermore, with the completion of several industrial parks, the agro processing and textiles sectors will experience high growths rates averaging 9.7% and 14.2% per year from 2020 to 2024, respectively, contributing to industrial growth",""],[1,"67","5","Made in Rwanda Industrial Promotion and Expansion","Establish and expand industries working with the private sector to promote locally produced materi- als and \"Made in Rwanda\" including: a pharmaceutical plant, a mosquito nets manufacturing plant, a chemical fertilizer plant & Industries for the production of constructions materials.",""],[1,"67","5","Priority Value Chain Development","Identify and develop priority value chains.",""],[1,"67","5","Business Process Outsourcing Service Development Programme","Establish a BPO service development program",""],[1,"67","5","Kigali Innovation City ICT Services Mechanism","leverage Kigali Innovation City as a mechanism to spur ICT services",""],[1,"68","1","BPO Finance Access Support","Facilitate BPO companies to access finance especially in the fields of accounting, legal and security services",""],[1,"68","1","Kigali BPO Park Master Developer Arrangement","Secure a master developer for Kigali BPO Park (infrastructure and real estate) and its anchor ten- ants.",""],[1,"68","4","Mineral Exploration and Resource Assessment","Upscale mining by completing exploration of potential mineral areas to establish the extent of national resources and reserves",""],[1,"68","4","Mineral and Quarry Value Addition Initiative","Prioritize increased value addition for mineral and quarry products to reach the international and local market expectations.",""],[1,"68","4","Tea Processing Capacity Expansion","Increase Tea processing factories in numbers and in capacity (from 15 to 19 factories).",""],[1,"69","1","Agro-Processing Raw Material Access and Industrial Blocs Initiative","Facilitate agro processing industries to access raw materials working with farmers and the private sector through improving the framework of contract farming and setting up of industrial blocs among others.",""],[1,"69","1","Coffee and Tree Crop Area Expansion","Expand coffee and tree cultivated area,",""]],"9":[[1,"13","11","Private and Public Investment Mobilization","This will require considerable efforts in boosting private and public investment financed by domestic savings and capital inflows;",""],[1,"20","1","Priority Value Chain Development and Investor Targeting","Identify and develop priority value chains.",""],[1,"25","6","MSME Entrepreneurship and Access to Resources Support Programme","This will be achieved by enhancing entrepreneurship and improving access to resources (such as finance, business advisory services, marketing platforms and equipment) for Micro, Small, and Medium-sized Enterprises (MSMEs) with strong job creation potential.",""],[1,"25","6","Anchor Investment and MSME Market Linkage Initiative","Anchor investments in various sectors will play a crucial role in creating backward and forward linkages to markets that support growth of MSMEs and generate employment.",""],[1,"26","3","Employment Mainstreaming in Public and Private Investments","deliberate strategies will be undertaken to mainstream employment creation into both public and private sector investments, with a focus on high-impact, labor-intensive projects.",""],[1,"66","2","Private Capital and Diverse Financing Products Mobilization","Attract private capital and diverse financing products through the Kigali International Financial Center, the capital market, and the financial sector at large",""]],"10":[[1,"35","9","Legislative Alignment of Finance Law with NST-2 Priorities","Enact and amend laws including the finance law (national budget) aligned with NST-2 priorities",""],[1,"36","2","Strategic Resource Prioritization Guidance","Provide strategic guidance to prioritization and :selected: allocation of resources",""],[1,"38","6","Expansion of Integrated Financial Management Information System to Sub-national Entities","This will be supported by creation of a critical mass of professional accountants and the roll out of Integrated Financial Management Information System (IFMIS) to sub- national entities including sectors (Imirenge), Districts Hospitals and health centers and schools.",""],[1,"38","7","District Revenue Capacity Enhancement and Local Tax Reform","Increase districts revenue capacity to finance their development needs by promoting local economic development and reforming laws on locally administered taxes and fees.",""],[1,"76","2","Public Financial Accountability and Audit Compliance Improvement","Increase the number of entities obtaining unqualified audit opinion on financial statements and compliance with laws and regulations",""],[1,"76","2","IFMIS Rollout and Accountant Training Programme","Train critical mass of professional accountants and roll out of Integrated Financial Management Information System (IFMIS) to sub-national entities",""],[1,"76","2","Local Revenue Capacity and Tax Reform","Increase districts revenue capacity to finance their development needs by promoting local economic development and reforming laws on locally administered taxes and fees",""],[1,"76","2","Oversight Institution Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen capabilities of OAG, RGB, RIB and Ombudsman in order to achieve greater institutional performance, delivery to citizens and compliance with accountability across public institutions",""]],"11":[[1,"13","2","Universal Access to Affordable Infrastructure and Services","Move Towards a Modern Rwandan Household through ensuring universal access to affordable and adequate infrastructure and services.",""],[1,"19","3","Electricity Access Expansion for Productive Users and Households","The scaling up of access to electricity will focus on connecting productive users (such as industries, commercial facilities, schools, health facilities, agro-processing plants, and other facilities) that contribute to socioeconomic development.",""],[1,"22","1","Electricity Network Upgrading and Loss Reduction Investments","Quality of electricity will be improved by continuing investments in network upgrading and strengthening as well as investing in loss reduction projects.",""],[1,"22","1","Productive Use Electricity Connection Expansion","Priority will be given to productive use connections such as industrial zones, market centers and other socio-economic facilities such as schools and health centers.",""],[1,"32","1","Universal Access to Basic Infrastructure","This will be achieved through Universal access to basic infrastructure such as electricity, water, sanitation and internet broadband.",""],[1,"32","2","National Electricity Access Scale-Up","Access to electricity will be scaled up to all from 34.4% (EICV5) to 100% by 2024 in collaboration with the private sector to reach off-grid areas and investments in grid expansion.",""],[1,"69","2","Electricity Generation Expansion and Service Quality Improvement","Scale up electricity generation and improve quality, affordability and reliability.",""],[1,"73","3","Off-Grid Electrification and Grid Expansion Investment","Collaborate with the private sector through off-grid connections and investments in grid expansion.",""]],"12":[[1,"19","8","Water Infrastructure Expansion and Rehabilitation Programme","This will involve expanding, rehabilitating and maintaining water infrastructure to improve the quality of water services delivered.",""],[1,"19","8","Planned Settlements Expansion for Water Service Delivery","This will be done in tandem with the scaling up of planned settlements to reach more households in a cost-efficient manner.",""],[1,"19","8","Water Treatment Plant Development and Maintenance","Daily water production capacity will be more than doubled to meet projected demand through the development and maintenance of water treatment plants.",""],[1,"19","8","Non-Revenue Water Reduction Initiative","Non-revenue water will be reduced to enhance efficiency in providing water services.",""],[1,"19","9","Universal Basic Water Access Expansion","The drive towards universal access to basic water will be accelerated for both productive use centers and households by ensuring water is accessible in all villages across the country.",""]],"13":[[1,"17","4","Agri-Hubs and Food Basket Site Management Models","New management models, such as Agri-hubs and Food Basket sites, will be adopted to enhance efficiency and maximize returns on agricultural investments.",""],[1,"17","4","Operationalization of Gabiro Agri-business Hub and Gako Beef","The operationalization of key projects, such as the Gabiro Agri- business Hub and Gako Beef, will be instrumental in achieving these goals.",""],[1,"23","7","Agricultural Value Chain Commercialization and Investment Promotion","Strengthen the commercialization of crop and animal resource value chains by increasing private sector engagement, promoting market-oriented agri-businesses, and capturing greater in-country surplus and value added.",""],[1,"24","1","Public-Private Partnership Promotion","through the promotion of public private partnerships (PPPs).",""],[1,"24","1","e-Soko+ Market Information System Strengthening and Expansion","The existing market information system, e-soko+ will be strengthened with the aim of expanding this service to provide ICT solutions to a broader set of challenges faced in the agricultural sector.",""],[1,"24","2","Agricultural Irrigation Expansion and Mechanization Scale-Up","Work with the private sector to increase the surface of consolidated and irrigated land and promote agricultural mechanization.",""],[1,"24","3","Irrigation Scheme Management Reform","Promote new models of irrigation scheme management, including the development and strengthening of farmers' and water users' associations, and the piloting and scaling up of public-private partnership models involving private service providers in managing irrigation schemes.",""],[1,"24","4","Terrace Expansion and Optimal Use Programme","Increases the land area covered by terraces and ensure their optimal use, land covered by radical terraces will increase from 110,905 ha (2017) to 142,500 ha by 2024.",""],[1,"24","4","Progressive Terrace Expansion Programme","Similarly, land covered by progressive terraces will increase from 923,604 ha (2017) to 1,007,624 ha by 2024.",""],[1,"24","5","Improved Seeds and Fertilizer Distribution System Reform","Review the system of management of distribution of inputs to ensure efficiency and timeliness in delivery working with the private sector and other stakeholders.",""],[1,"24","6","Crop Seed Research and Local Seed Production Scale-Up","Promote research and develop new seed varieties.",""],[1,"24","6","Agricultural Extension Services Expansion","the extension services program will be expanded through the Twigire-Muhinzi model.",""],[1,"25","2","Post-Harvest Handling and Storage Infrastructure Development","Work with the private sector to build post-harvest handling and storage facilities across the country and to add value to agricultural produce (processing).",""],[1,"25","3","High-Value Crop Production Scale-Up","Scale up the production of high-value crops including: horticulture (flowers, vegetables, fruits), among others",""],[1,"25","6","Agricultural Ecosystem Financing Program","A comprehensive agricultural ecosystem financing program including lease financing and insurance with a focus on priority value chains will be established.",""],[1,"49","5","Agricultural Technology Efficiency Support","To improve labor productivity, public expenditure will be directed towards improving the education system, supporting technological efforts to realize efficiency gains in land and agriculture, and enhancing the quality of infrastructure.",""],[1,"50","4","Climate-Resilient Farming Methods Investment","These gains will come from investments in improved farming methods such as the adoption of climate resilient techniques.",""],[1,"50","4","Agricultural Value Chain Linkage Development","Developing stronger value chain linkages with both domestic and export markets will allow for larger supplies of domestic agricultural products to be used as",""],[1,"70","2","Agricultural Value Chain Commercialization and Productivity Support","Strengthen the commercialization of crop and animal resource value chains",""],[1,"70","2","Agricultural Land Consolidation and Mechanization Initiative","Work with the private sector to increase the surface of consolidated and irrigated land and promote agricultural mechanization",""],[1,"70","2","Irrigation Scheme Management Reform","Promote new models of irrigation scheme management",""],[1,"70","2","Agricultural Input Distribution Management Reform","Review the system of management of distribution of inputs working with the private sector",""],[1,"70","2","Seed Research and Development Programme","Promote Research and develop new seed varieties",""],[1,"70","2","Agricultural Extension Services Scale-Up","Scale up Twigire-Muhinzi model to increase extension services",""],[1,"70","2","Post-Harvest Storage and Value Addition Investment","Work with the private sector to build post-harvest handling and storage facilities and value addition to agricultural produce",""],[1,"70","2","High-Value Crop Production Expansion","Scale up the production of high-value crops including: horticulture: (flowers, vegetables, fruits), among others",""],[1,"70","2","Agricultural Ecosystem Financing Program","Establish a comprehensive agricultural ecosystem financing program including lease financing and insurance with a focus on priority value chains",""]],"14":[[1,"17","6","Livestock and Aquaculture Value Chain Scaling","production and productivity will be increased by scaling up key value chains in livestock and aquaculture.",""],[1,"17","6","Modern Livestock Farming Practices Adoption","This will involve adopting modern livestock farming practices such as zero grazing, increasing access to improved breeds, ensuring adequate water infrastructure and management for livestock.",""],[1,"17","6","Animal Feed Production and Dairy Infrastructure Investment","Strategic interventions will also focus on boosting domestic production of animal feeds, and investing in the dairy sector by establishing modern animal hubs and expanding the capacity of milk collection centers.",""],[1,"25","4","Livestock Farmer Professionalization and Productivity Improvement Program","Establish a program to improve professionalization of livestock farmers and increase their output in terms of quality, volume and productivity.",""],[1,"25","4","Livestock Drought Resilience Infrastructure and Fodder Storage Expansion","Furthermore, the construction of dams and boreholes for livestock in drought prone areas will be scaled up and promoted as well as the storage of animal fodder.",""],[1,"25","5","Livestock Subsector Flagship Investment Projects","Attract private sector and farmers to invest in flagship projects in the livestock sub sector including: the construction and operationalization of Milk Collection Centers (MCCs), modern fish farming, animal feeds production, Gako beef farm, processing and value addition of leather.",""],[1,"70","2","Livestock Farmer Professionalization Programme","Establish a program to improve professionalization of livestock farmers to increase their productivity",""],[1,"70","2","Livestock Flagship Investment Mobilization","Attract private sector and farmers to invest in flagship projects in the livestock sub sector",""]],"15":[[1,"13","11","Tradable Goods and Services Production Support","and sustained efforts to boost production of tradable goods and services.",""],[1,"18","2","Export Market Access Facilitation and SME Export Aggregation","Exporters will be facilitated in accessing international markets, while aggregating exports of SME products to capitalize on economies of scale.",""],[1,"18","2","National Quality Infrastructure and One-Stop Center Strengthening","the national quality infrastructure framework will be streamlined and the one-stop center strengthened to facilitate investors attain the required domestic and export market standards.",""],[1,"18","2","E-Commerce Readiness Program for SMEs","Furthermore, an E-commerce Readiness Program will be implemented to help SMEs leverage digital trade platforms for exports.",""],[1,"22","2","Export Growth Fund Scale-Up and Reform","Scale up and reform the export growth fund to increase access to finance for exporters.",""]],"16":[[1,"18","3","Logistics Infrastructure Development for Trade and Export Growth","Investments will also support the development of logistics infrastructure crucial for facilitating trade and export growth.",""],[1,"18","3","Cold Chain Infrastructure Upgrade","Cold chain development will be augmented by investing in required infrastructure such as cold storage facilities and improved transportation networks, while adopting modern technology like temperature-controlled logistics and digital tracking platforms.",""],[1,"18","3","Kigali Logistics Platform and Wholesale Market Development","This includes completing the Kigali Logistics Platform (KLP) and developing the Kigali wholesale market for horticultural products.",""],[1,"21","4","Trade Facilitation and Business Cost Reduction Projects","Reduce the cost of doing business and facilitate trade by implementing key projects:",""],[1,"21","5","Railway Connection Planning and Construction","Finalize planning for an appropriate railway connection and initiate construction.",""],[1,"21","8","Kigali Logistics Platform and Bonded Warehouses Development","Operationalize Kigali Logistics Platform, bonded warehouses and work with private sector to develop international transport and logistics companies.",""],[1,"21","9","Cross-Border Market Construction Programme","Construct new modern cross border markets to facilitate cross border trade.",""],[1,"21","10","Lake Kivu Port Construction","Construct ports on Lake Kivu in Rusizi, Nyamasheke, Karongi and Rubavu districts working with private sector",""],[1,"21","11","Foreign Multi-Service Centers Operationalization","Operationalize foreign multi service centers.",""],[1,"43","6","Joint Infrastructure Flagship Projects for Trade Facilitation","Further mobilization of resources to implement joint infrastructure flagship projects to facilitate trade.",""],[1,"49","5","Infrastructure Quality Enhancement Investment","To improve labor productivity, public expenditure will be directed towards improving the education system, supporting technological efforts to realize efficiency gains in land and agriculture, and enhancing the quality of infrastructure.",""],[1,"51","2","Infrastructure Investment and Construction Expansion","Construction will also experience substantial growth with an average rate of 11.4% per year 2017 to 2024 due to the high levels of infrastructure investment envisaged in the NST1, including construction of Bugesera international airport",""],[1,"66","5","Rural and Urban Transport Service Improvement","Improve rural and urban transportation services",""],[1,"66","5","Public Lighting Installation on National and District Roads","Install Public lighting on major national and district roads.",""],[1,"69","2","Railway Connection Planning and Construction","Finalize planning for an appropriate railway connection and initiate construction.",""],[1,"69","2","National Roads Construction Programme","Construct National asphalt roads",""],[1,"69","2","Feeder Roads Construction, Rehabilitation and Maintenance","Construct, rehabilitate and maintain feeder roads.",""],[1,"69","2","Kigali Logistics Platform and Bonded Warehouses Operationalization","Operationalize Kigali Logistics Platform, bonded warehouses and work with private sector to devel- op international transport and logistics companies.",""],[1,"69","2","Cross-Border Market Construction Programme","Construct new modern cross border markets to facilitate cross border trade.",""],[1,"69","2","Lake Kivu Port Construction Programme","Construct ports in Lake Kivu in Rusizi, Nyamasheke, Karongi and Rubavu districts working with private sector",""],[1,"69","2","Foreign Multi-Service Centers Operationalization","Operationalize foreign multi service centers.",""],[1,"69","2","Industrial Parks and Special Economic Zone Expansion","Construct and develop industrial parks in provinces and expand the Kigali Special Economic Zone",""]],"17":[[1,"18","7","Nationwide Tourism Destination Development Programme","New and existing tourism destinations will be developed nationwide to diversify tourist attractions with a strong focus on promoting nature-based tourism.",""],[1,"18","7","Tourism and Conservation Financing Initiative","Innovative tourism and conservation financing initiatives such as Green Bonds, investments in conservation, public-private partnerships, and product diversification, will support this and elevate Rwanda into a high-end tourism market.",""],[1,"20","5","Tourism Infrastructure Investment and Kivu Belt Tourism Master Plan","Increasing investments in tourism infrastructure including the development of the Kivu Belt tourism master plan;",""],[1,"20","6","Hospitality Industry Development and Private Sector Capacity Building","Developing the hospitality industry and build the capacity of the private sector to provide high levels of service delivery.",""],[1,"20","7","MICE Tourism Promotion and Rwanda Convention Bureau Strengthening","Accelerating MICE tourism growth by attracting big events and conferences and developing cultural and religious tourism working with the private sector.",""],[1,"67","5","MICE and Sport Tourism Promotion","Attract large events, exhibitions, and meetings to grow MICE and sport tourism",""],[1,"68","1","National Tourism Master Plan Development","Develop a new tourism master plan and work with the private sector to diversify products nationwide to grow leisure and domestic tourism",""],[1,"68","1","Kivu Belt Tourism Master Plan","Develop the Kivu Belt tourism master plan;",""],[1,"68","1","Events, Conferences, and Cultural Tourism Promotion","Attract big events and conferences and develop cultural and religious tourism working with the private sector",""],[1,"68","1","Kigali Convention Bureau Strengthening","Strengthen Kigali Convention Bureau to enable it play a leading role in attracting big events and conferences and ensuring the branding of Rwanda as a world class conference destination.",""],[1,"68","2","Visit Rwanda Partnerships Promotion Initiative","Leverage existing and new Visit Rwanda Partnerships ( in sport, creative industry, entertainment, for example) to promote tourism, investment, and MICE",""],[1,"68","4","MICE Services Professionalization and Certification Programme","Raise the quality of MICE related services through professionalization programs, standards and certification to increase average spending per visitor",""],[1,"69","1","Innovative Tourism and Conservation Financing Mechanism","Mobilize innovative tourism and conservation financing (green bonds, PPPs etc)",""]],"18":[[1,"11","1","Kigali Convention Centre Conference Hub Development","a state-of-the-art conference hub in the Kigali Convention Centre",""],[1,"18","8","MICE Industry Professionalization and Standards Program","The MICE industry will be enhanced through professionalization programs alongside the introduction of industrial standards and certification to raise the overall quality of services offered.",""],[1,"18","8","Strategic Event Attraction and Partnership Development for MICE","the country will attract events aligned with national priorities, including high-level meetings, strategic partnerships, and sports events.",""]],"19":[[1,"18","9","National Sports Infrastructure Expansion","To support this, sports infrastructure will be expanded nationwide, facilitating community-level sports activities and aiding in identifying and nurturing top talent in partnership with key stakeholders, including the private sector.",""],[1,"33","3","Recreational Activities and Sports Promotion","Promote recreational activities and sports for all to increase the socioeconomic impact of sports facilities to the citizens.",""],[1,"33","3","Private Sector Stadium Construction and Management","Private sector will be engaged in the construction and management of stadia including Gahanga Sports Complex, Ngoma, Bugesera and Nyagatare stadiums.",""],[1,"71","2","Private Sector Investment in Sports Development","Attract private sector investment in sports development",""],[1,"71","5","International Sports Events Hosting Initiative","Create, attract and host international sports events",""],[1,"72","1","Accessible Community Sports Spaces and Facilities","Create accessible community sports spaces and related sports facilities;",""],[1,"72","3","Youth Center and Multi-Discipline Sports Facility Development","Establish and improve youth centers equipped with multi discipline sports facilities at decentralized level",""]],"20":[[1,"19","4","Least-Cost Power Development Planning","Energy generation will be aligned with projected demand and economic forecasts based on the least-cost power development plan.",""],[1,"19","5","Renewable and Clean Energy Expansion","The energy transition will prioritize increasing the share of renewable and clean energy in the power generation mix from 51% to 60%",""],[1,"19","5","Nuclear Technology Development for Productive Uses","Nuclear technology for productive uses in sectors such as health, energy and agriculture among others will be explored and developed",""],[1,"19","6","Critical Energy Products Reserves and Storage Capacity Development","To ensure long-term energy security, adequate reserves and storage capacity for critical energy products such as oil and gas, will be developed and maintained.",""],[1,"21","13","Electricity Generation Scale-Up and Power Supply Improvement","Scale up electricity generation and improve quality, affordability and reliability.",""]],"21":[[1,"19","5","Clean and Efficient Biomass Cooking Technology Scale-Up","while scaling up the adoption of clean and efficient biomass cooking technologies for large- scale users (e.g. schools, health facilities, prisons, etc.) and households",""],[1,"19","5","Cleaner Fuel Promotion for Industrial and Household Use","Development and use of cleaner fuels such as methane gas for industrial and home uses will also be promoted",""]],"22":[[1,"11","1","Road Network Maintenance and Expansion","a well maintained and expanding road network in urban and rural areas",""],[1,"18","8","Scheduled Bus Route Expansion","Improve rural and urban transportation services through the establishment of 14,100km (13,932.5km currently) of scheduled bus routes countrywide.",""],[1,"18","8","Kigali Dedicated Bus Lane Construction","In Kigali city, 22 km of dedicated bus lines will be constructed.",""],[1,"21","6","National Asphalt Roads Construction Programme","Construct 800 km of National asphalt roads including: Ngoma-Bugesera-Nyanza, Base-Gicumbi-Rukomo-Nyagatare, Huye-Kibeho-Munini, Kagitumba-Kayonza- Rusumo and Kigali Ring road.",""],[1,"21","7","Feeder Road Construction, Rehabilitation and Maintenance Programme","Construct, rehabilitate and maintain 3,000km of feeder roads.",""]],"23":[[1,"11","1","Air Connectivity Expansion","include vastly improved air connectivity",""],[1,"20","5","RwandAir Capacity Expansion","The aviation sector will be expanded by scaling up RwandAir's capacity, aiming to double the number of passengers transported by the national carrier, increase the number of destinations, and boost cargo freight capacity and services to facilitate exports.",""],[1,"20","5","Bugesera International Airport Completion and Operationalization","This will be complemented by the completion and operationalization of the new Bugesera International Airport and the development of subsidiary airports.",""],[1,"20","9","RwandAir Network Expansion","Expansion of RwandAir to connect Rwanda to Africa, Europe, America and Asia;",""],[1,"21","1","Bugesera Airport Phase 1 Completion and Operationalization","Completion and operationalization of Bugesera Airport phase 1 with a capacity of 1.7 million passengers annually and develop backward and forward linkages to local industries,",""],[1,"21","2","Aviation Center of Excellence","Establishing a center of excellence in aviation to develop critical skills in the sector",""],[1,"21","3","Airport Rehabilitation and Expansion","Rehabilitation of Kamembe airport and expansion of Rubavu airport",""],[1,"51","3","Bugesera International Airport Completion","These growth rates will be driven by the completion of Bugesera international airport and the continued expansion of Rwandair routes.",""],[1,"51","3","Rwandair Route Expansion","These growth rates will be driven by the completion of Bugesera international airport and the continued expansion of Rwandair routes.",""],[1,"68","2","RwandAir Network Expansion","Expand RwandAir to connect Africa to Europe, America and Asia;",""],[1,"68","2","Bugesera Airport Phase 1 Completion and Linkage Development","complete and operationalize Bugesera Airport phase 1 and develop backward and forward linkages to local industries,",""],[1,"68","2","Aviation Center of Excellence","Establish a center of excellence in aviation to develop critical skills in the sector",""],[1,"68","2","Airport Rehabilitation and Expansion Programme","Rehabilitate Kamembe airport and expand Rubavu airport",""]],"24":[[1,"18","7","Local Construction Materials Development Initiative","Promote and develop Local construction materials in collaboration with the private sector in line with the 'Made in Rwanda' policy to support the growth of the construction sector and the affordable and low cost housing programme.",""],[1,"20","9","Detailed Physical Planning and Site Servicing Programme","the development of detailed physical plans, site servicing and provision of basic infrastructure will be expedited to enhance well- planned urban and rural settlements",""],[1,"20","9","Informal Settlement Upgrading Programme","Informal settlements will be upgraded through various approaches including providing basic infrastructure services and rehousing in collaboration with the concerned communities",""],[1,"20","9","Relocation to Resilient Settlements Initiative","Households in high-risk zones will be urged to relocate to more resilient sites while those in scattered rural settlements will be mobilized to settle in planned settlements",""],[1,"21","1","Affordable Housing Expansion Programme","Development of affordable housing for rent and/or purchase will be expanded in the Cok, as well as satellite and secondary cities in partnership with the private sector to meet diverse demand across income segments.",""],[1,"32","13","Relocation and Planned Settlement Support Programme","Develop and facilitate decent settlement of Rwandans including relocation of those living in high-risk zones.",""],[1,"32","13","Affordable and Sustainable Housing Model Development","This will be further enhanced through: development of affordable and sustainable housing models for urban and rural areas that can be scaled up drawing from the experience of the",""],[1,"33","1","Integrated Development Program Model Villages and Rural Settlement Planning","Integrated Development Program (IDP) model villages, review and elaboration of rural settlements lay out plans.",""],[1,"33","2","Affordable Housing Fund Operationalization","The affordable housing fund will be operationalized to facilitate citizens acquire affordable and decent housing.",""],[1,"66","5","Flagship Projects for Secondary Cities and Key Urban Areas","Develop Flagship projects in secondary cities and other key urban areas to support thriving and sustainable urban economies.",""],[1,"66","5","Secondary City Master Plan Update","Update Master plans of secondary cities and other key towns.",""],[1,"66","5","Local Construction Materials Development Initiative","Promote and develop Local construction materials in collaboration with the private sector in line with the 'Made in Rwanda' policy.",""],[1,"66","5","Basic Infrastructure Development for New Residential Zones and Urban Roads","Develop Basic infrastructure through servicing of new residential zones and upgrading of unpaved urban roads",""],[1,"73","3","Decent Settlement and Affordable Housing Development","Develop and facilitate decent settlement of Rwandans including relocation of those living in high-risk zones and development of affordable and sustainable housing models for urban and rural areas",""],[1,"73","3","Affordable Housing Fund Operationalization","Operationalize the affordable housing fund to facilitate citizens to acquire affordable and decent housing",""]],"25":[[1,"11","1","National Fiber Optic Rollout and ICT Adoption","country-wide fiber optic roll out and rapid adoption of ICT",""],[1,"19","4","National Digital Literacy Program","Ensure digital literacy for all youth (16 to 30 years) by 2024 through implementation of a national digital literacy program",""],[1,"19","4","Local Digital Content Development and Device Access Initiative","This will be supplemented by initiatives to develop local contents and facilitate citizens (including people with disabilities) to access digital devices that will enable them use online services.",""],[1,"20","2","BPO Services Development Program","A BPO services development program will be established to capitalize on previous investments in fiber optic.",""],[1,"20","2","BPO Skills Upgrading Support for Universities and Education Centers","supporting universities and education centers to upgrade skills related to BPO services,",""],[1,"20","2","BPO Finance Access Support","facilitating BPO companies to access finance especially in the fields of accounting, legal and security services,",""],[1,"20","2","Kigali BPO Park Development and Anchor Tenant Securing","securing a master developer for Kigali BPO park (infrastructure and real estate) and its anchor tenants.",""],[1,"21","8","Digital Literacy Expansion Programme","digital literacy is planned to increase from 53% to 100%, equipping the Rwandan population with the necessary skills to fully benefit from digital transformation.",""],[1,"21","8","Coder Training and Advanced ICT Skills Programme","To develop skills for the ICT sector and prepare the youth for future jobs, 1 million coders will be trained and 500,000 people will be equipped with advanced ICT skills.",""],[1,"21","9","Universal Smart Device Ownership and Affordable Connectivity Initiative","In partnership with the private sector, efforts will focus on ensuring universal smart device ownership and affordable, quality connectivity nationwide to foster the adoption and use of digital technology by all Rwandans, enabled by best-in-class ICT infrastructure capabilities including high-performance computing environments that positions Rwanda as a proof-of-concept hub.",""],[1,"32","12","National Broadband and 4G Network Rollout","Broadband coverage will be rolled out to all citizens through the roll out of the 4G network, promoting internet of things and increase in smart devices penetration.",""],[1,"35","3","Digital and Soft Skills Development Programme","digital and other soft skills development",""],[1,"67","2","Digital Content and Device Access Support","Develop local contents and facilitate citizens (including people with disabilities) to access digital devices that will enable them use online services.",""],[1,"73","3","National Broadband and 4G Network Expansion","Scale up broadband coverage to all citizens through the roll out of the 4G network, promoting internet of things and increase smart devices penetration",""]],"26":[[1,"12","6","Domestic Savings Mobilization and Financial Services Hub Development","Increase domestic savings and position Rwanda as a hub for financial services to promote investments.",""],[1,"22","4","Expansion of Formal Financial Services and Digital Payments","the financial sector will aim to enhance its contribution to overall growth and the economic well-being of Rwandans. This will be achieved by expanding the use of formal financial services, including digital and electronic payment systems, with a particular focus on youth and women.",""],[1,"22","4","Financial Education and Literacy Strengthening","These initiatives will be supported by improved financial education and literacy alongside the diversification of financial services and products to better meet consumer needs.",""],[1,"22","4","Financial Sector Regulatory and Institutional Capacity Strengthening","Moreover, creating a conducive regulatory environment and building financial literacy will encourage savings and investment from a broader segment of the population. Strengthening the capacity of local financial institutions and improving access to digital financial services will play a key role in deepening financial inclusion and ensuring that capital is effectively channeled into productive investments",""],[1,"23","2","Collective Investment Scheme Product Diversification","diversify the number of Collective Investment Scheme products available to investors, offering a broader range of investment options to encourage participation in the financial market.",""],[1,"23","2","Financial Services Center Development Initiative","Develop Rwanda into a financial services center.",""],[1,"23","3","Umurenge SACCO Automation and Digital Financial Services Sensitization","This will be supported by automation of Umurenge SACCOs and implementing a series of sensitizations to increase uptake of electronic and digital financial services.",""],[1,"23","4","Consolidation of SACCOs into a Cooperative Bank","Supporting local economic development will also be a priority through the consolidation of Umurenge Savings and Credit Cooperative Organizations (SACCOs) at district and national levels into a cooperative bank, which can improve access and provide tailored financial services to local communities and small businesses while leveraging the use of technology.",""],[1,"23","4","Financial Inclusion Expansion","Bring financial services closer to people by increasing the percentage of adult Rwandans financially included at 100% by 2024 (from 89% in 2017).",""],[1,"23","5","Capital Market Development and Financing Diversification","Develop the capital market and increase dynamism in line with the ten-year capital market master plan.",""],[1,"23","6","Long-Term Savings and Pension Scheme Expansion","Operationalize long-term savings scheme and pension for all Rwandans including those in the informal sector as a basis to support long-term domestic investments.",""],[1,"48","4","Innovative Savings Mobilization Schemes","Through financial sector development, including the introduction of innovative savings mobilization schemes, the private domestic savings rate is projected to increase from 12.1% in 2017 to 23.9% in 2024.",""],[1,"50","3","Foreign Exchange Reserve Build-up","It will also be necessary to allow for interest payments on foreign capital and to encourage the gradual build-up of adequate foreign exchange reserves in the banking system.",""],[1,"69","5","Financial Sector Skills and Investor Incentive Measures","Develop specialized skills and establish incentive mechanisms to attract investors in the financial sector.",""],[1,"69","5","Umurenge SACCO Automation and Digital Financial Services Uptake","Ensure automation of Umurenge SACCOs and implement a series of sensitizations to increase uptake of electronic and digital financial services.",""],[1,"69","5","Private Sector Financial Innovation and Inclusion Expansion","Work with the private sector to scale up & develop innovative financial services to increase financial inclusion among the population.",""],[1,"69","5","Capital Market Master Plan Implementation","Develop the capital market through implementation of the ten-year capital market master plan.",""],[1,"69","5","Universal Long-Term Savings and Pension Operationalization","Operationalize long-term savings and pension for all Rwandans.",""],[1,"69","5","Long-Term Investment Fund Expansion","Expand Long term investment funds through mobilization and investment of Agaciro Development Fund (AgDF) as well as promotion of collective investment schemes through Rwanda National Investment Trust (RNIT).",""]],"27":[[1,"26","1","Public Forest Allocation to Private Operators","Continue to strengthen forest management and ensure their sustainable exploitation working with the private sector.",""],[1,"26","2","Forest Landscape Restoration and Reforestation Programme","The area covered by forest will be increased and sustained at 30% till 2024 from 29.6% in 2017 through forest landscape restoration.",""],[1,"26","3","Promotion of Alternative Cooking Fuels","This will be achieved by focusing on promoting use of alternative fuels such as cooking gas and biogas.",""],[1,"70","5","Sustainable Forest Management and Restoration","Continue to strengthen forest management and ensure their sustainable exploitation working with the private sector.",""],[1,"70","5","Forest Landscape Restoration","Increase and sustain area covered by forest through forest landscape restoration.",""],[1,"70","5","Alternative Cooking Fuel Promotion","Promote use of alternative fuels such as cooking gas and biogas.",""]],"28":[[1,"13","11","Land Efficiency and Innovation Enhancement","achieving significant increases in land efficiency and innovative capacity;",""]],"29":[[1,"25","2","Climate and Nature Finance Mobilization","At least USD 3 billion in climate and nature finance will be mobilized to support nature conservation and climate mitigation and adaptation initiatives.",""]],"30":[[1,"17","11","Youth and Women Entrepreneurship and Finance Access Support","Support and empower youth and women to create business through entrepreneurship and access to finance.",""],[1,"17","12","Workplace Learning Partnership Programme","Develop and enhance strategic partnerships with private sector companies in the implementation of Work Place Learning (Rapid Response Training, Industrial based training and apprenticeship).",""],[1,"18","1","Labor Market Information System Update and Skills Identification","This will be done through working with the private sector to update the Labor Market Information System (LMIS) and identify critical skills required in the labor market to inform training programs in TVET.",""],[1,"18","2","Employment Planning Mainstreaming and NEP Coordination, Implementation, and Monitoring","Mainstream employment planning into all key sectors of the economy and strengthen the coordination, implementation and monitoring of the National Employment Programme (NEP).",""],[1,"18","3","Model Income and Employment-Generating Project Support Mechanism","Develop a mechanism to support at least one model income and employment- generating project in each village.",""],[1,"25","6","Youth and Women Employment Initiatives","Special focus will be placed on employment initiatives for youth and women, leveraging community-based approaches in infrastructure, environmental protection and agricultural extension programs.",""],[1,"35","3","Youth and Women's Entrepreneurship Support","more focus will be on promoting youth and women's entrepreneurship",""],[1,"66","2","Youth and Women Entrepreneurship Finance Support","Support and empower youth and women to create businesses through entrepreneurship and access to finance.",""],[1,"66","2","Workplace Learning Partnership Programme","Develop and enhance strategic partnerships with private sector companies in the implementation of Work Place Learning.",""],[1,"66","2","National Employment Programme Coordination and Monitoring","Mainstream employment planning in key sectors of the economy and strengthen the coordination, implementation and monitoring of the National Employment Programme (NEP).",""],[1,"66","2","Village Model Income and Employment Project Mechanism","Develop a mechanism to support at least one model income and employment-generating project in each village",""],[1,"74","2","Employment Creation Mainstreaming in Investments","Mainstream employment creation in Public and private investments with high impact and labor intensity",""],[1,"74","5","Workplace Learning and Youth Employability Strengthening","Improve & Strengthen synergies in workplace learning, employability skills for youth, job-matching services and labour market systems [through internships, apprenticeships, re-skilling and up-skilling among others]",""]],"31":[[1,"19","5","Centers of Excellence Establishment and Operationalization","Support the establishment and operationalization of new and existing Centers of Excellence with a focus on science, technology and innovation.",""],[1,"26","1","Strategic Investment Projects for Jobs and Skills Development","major public and private investments projects like Bugesera International Airport, the Aviation Skills Academy, Industrial Parks, the Gabiro Agri-hub, the Nyagatare Milk Powder Plant and sport complexes will serve as platforms for employment and skills development.",""],[1,"26","1","Internships, Apprenticeships, and Re-skilling Initiatives","Synergies between workplace learning, employability skills for youth, and labor market systems will be strengthened through initiatives such as internships, apprenticeships and re-skilling programs.",""],[1,"26","2","Critical Sectors Talent Pool Development","In parallel, a talent pool will be developed for critical sectors such as Global Business Services (GBS) companies, financial services center, health, engineering, and more.",""],[1,"26","2","Specialized Skills Development for Service Sectors","Specialized skills including technology, communication and electrical motor maintenance will further drive the growth of job-rich, productive service sectors.",""],[1,"26","3","Labor Market Information System Improvement","Labor market information systems will be improved to match job opportunities with job seekers better, ensuring efficient workforce planning and employment growth.",""],[1,"28","4","Technical Secondary Schools Centers of Excellence","Technical Secondary Schools (TSS) centers of Excellence will be established in all districts to scale up modern, high-quality training nationwide.",""],[1,"28","4","Expansion of Vocational Training Centers Through Workplace Learning","Vocational Training Centers (VTCs) through workplace learning approaches will be scaled up in every cell in the country.",""],[1,"28","5","TVET and Higher Learning Institutions Modernization","Technical Vocational Education and Training (TVET) and Higher Learning Institutions (HLIs) will be continuously improved with modern infrastructure, equipment and provisioned with adequate consumables and materials to enhance STEM learning and promote research and innovation aligned to labor market demands.",""],[1,"31","5","Technical and Vocational Education and Training Promotion","Technical and Vocational Education and Training (TVET) will further be promoted.",""],[1,"31","6","STEM Promotion Across All Levels of Education","Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics (STEM) across all levels of education will be promoted at all levels.",""],[1,"35","2","Capacity Development and Retention Initiatives","NST2 will promote comprehensive initiatives targeting institutions, and people and creating an enabling environment for capacity enhancement and retention.",""],[1,"35","3","Sector-Specific Critical and Emerging Skills Training","supporting sector- specific training in critical skills and emerging technologies, such as AI, big data analytics, and green technologies",""],[1,"40","7","Workforce Capacity Development Initiatives","Public and private institutions will undertake capacity development initiatives for their workforce.",""],[1,"66","2","Priority Sub-Sector Development Support","Develop and support priority sub-sectors with high potential for growth and employment",""],[1,"66","2","Workplace Learning Partnership Programme","Develop and enhance strategic partnerships with private sector companies in the implementation of Work Place Learning.",""],[1,"66","2","TVET Labour Market Relevance Enhancement","Increase the number of TVET graduates with skills relevant to the labor market.",""],[1,"67","2","Kigali Innovation City Skills Ecosystem Development","Develop and operationalize a thriving skills ecosystem for attracting and nurturing local and interna- tional talent around the Kigali Innovation City (KIC) model.",""],[1,"67","2","National Digital Literacy Programme","Implement the national digital literacy program",""],[1,"67","2","Centers of Excellence Establishment and Operationalization","Support the establishment and operationalization of new and existing Centers of Excellence with a focus on science, technology and innovation.",""],[1,"67","2","Applied Skills Partnership Strengthening","Reinforce partnership with these sectors to build skills with practical application in: health, education, industry, cyber security among others.",""],[1,"67","2","Research and Development Promotion for Economic Transformation","Promote research and development to fast-track Rwanda's economic transformation especially in the area of technology for industrial development",""],[1,"68","1","Hospitality Sector Capacity-Building Programme","Develop the hospitality industry and build the capacity of the private sector to provide high levels of service delivery.",""],[1,"68","2","Aviation Center of Excellence","Establish a center of excellence in aviation to develop critical skills in the sector",""],[1,"73","1","Technical and Vocational Education and Training Promotion","Promote Technical and Vocational Education and Training (TVET)",""],[1,"73","1","STEM Student Attraction and Research Capacity Expansion","Identify and attract the most excellent and suitable students for STEM, · Increase the capacity of STEM research centers and science schools",""]],"32":[[1,"30","5","Major Sanitation Infrastructure Projects","Major sanitation projects will be implemented to support the sustainability of cities and urban areas.",""],[1,"30","6","Public Sanitation Facilities Expansion","Public sanitation facilities will continue to be scaled up in public and private facilities to cater to the sanitation needs of all individuals with a focus on inclusivity and convenience.",""],[1,"31","1","Community Hygiene and Tailored Sanitation Promotion","Communities and households will be mobilized to continuously adopt safe and modern hygiene and sanitation practices for disease prevention.",""],[1,"31","1","Private-Sector Collaboration for Household Sanitation Solutions","Tailor-made sanitation solutions for different households will be promoted in collaboration with the private sector.",""],[1,"32","3","Water Supply System Expansion and Rehabilitation","Access to water will be scaled up to all from 87.4% (EICV5) to 100% by 2024 through investments in: Construction, extension, rehabilitation of 1,937 Km of water supply systems in city of Kigali and other towns, and of 1,851 Km of water supply systems in rural areas and Daily water production capacity shall be increased from 182,120 to 303,120 cubic meters per day.",""],[1,"32","4","Sanitation and Hygiene Scale-Up","Access to sanitation and hygiene will be scaled up to all from 86.2% (EICV5) to 100%",""],[1,"32","4","Waste Management Systems Development","waste management systems will be developed in cities, towns and rural areas.",""],[1,"32","5","Household Toilet Construction Standards Development","Development of the standards for the construction of household toilets",""],[1,"32","6","Public Toilet Construction","Construction of public toilets (public institutions, commercial premises, etc.)",""],[1,"32","7","Kigali Centralized Sewerage System Construction","Construction of Kigali Centralized Sewerage System (120,000m3/d)",""],[1,"32","8","Kigali Faecal Sludge Treatment Plant Construction","Construction of Kigali faecal sludge treatment plant (1000m3/d)",""],[1,"32","9","Semi-Centralized Sewerage System Rehabilitation and Upgrading","Rehabilitation and upgrading of semi-centralized sewerage system in Kigali Estates",""],[1,"32","10","Semi-Centralized Sewerage System Construction","Construction of Semi centralized sewerage systems in all planned and grouped settlements",""],[1,"32","11","District Landfill Construction and Waste Treatment Facilities","Construction of modern landfills in all districts and, putting in place waste treatment facilities.",""],[1,"73","3","Water Supply System Construction and Rehabilitation","Ensure universal access to water through Construction, extension & rehabilitation of water supply systems in urban and rural areas.",""],[1,"73","3","Urban and Rural Waste Management Systems","Develop waste management systems in cities, towns and rural areas.",""]],"33":[[1,"12","13","Strategic Investments in Education Access and Quality","Focus will be on strategic investments in all levels of education",""],[1,"13","11","Education Improvement Initiative","massive improvements in education;",""],[1,"27","10","Inclusive Access and Education Quality Improvement","the education sector will focus on strengthening inclusive access, particularly in pre-primary and improving the quality of education at all levels.",""],[1,"28","1","Basic Education Quality Improvement Programme","In basic education, the emphasis will be on improving quality through providing adequate learning materials, enhanced teacher recruitment, training and management, expanding infrastructure to increase hours of learning, and reducing classroom overcrowding and the distances traveled by students to reach school.",""],[1,"28","2","Education Enrolment and Progression Support Mechanisms","mechanisms will be strengthened to ensure timely enrolment and progression at all levels of education.",""],[1,"28","2","Dropout Reduction and Attendance Monitoring Initiative","Emphasis will be put on lowering primary and secondary dropout rates through enhanced attendance monitoring and tracking, sustaining the school feeding program, community mobilization and addressing the root causes of drop outs.",""],[1,"28","2","School Feeding Programme","sustaining the school feeding program",""],[1,"28","3","Learning Outcomes Improvement Initiative","Additionally, there will be a strong focus on improving learning outcomes, especially in mathematics, science, and languages.",""],[1,"28","3","Education ICT Scale-Up","The use of ICT across the education sector will be scaled up.",""],[1,"30","5","Pre-Primary Education Expansion Programme","Ensure access to pre-primary education so as to increase pre-primary net enrolment rate from 17.5% (2016) to 45% by 2024.",""],[1,"30","5","Standardized Early Childhood Education School Rollout","This will be achieved through providing standardized Early Childhood Education schools in all villages through partnership with private sector, communities and putting in place public- private partnership models for ECE and ECDs to enhance cost-effective rollout.",""],[1,"30","5","Lower Primary Foundational Skills Strengthening","The provision of education at lower primary level will be strengthened so that children develop better foundational skills in Kinyarwanda, English and Mathematics to enable them perform well at upper primary and secondary levels.",""],[1,"30","6","School Infrastructure and Learning Materials Upgrade","Upgrading and increasing school infrastructure and ensuring access to adequate equipment including modern laboratories, and appropriate teaching and modern learning materials.",""],[1,"31","1","Community-Based Classroom Construction Mobilization","mobilizing the population in the construction of classrooms using Umuganda and other community-based activities.",""],[1,"31","2","Teacher In-Service Training and Welfare Support","This will be done through in-service education in learner-centered trainings, provision of incentives will be undertaken to attract brilliant students to join the teaching profession and retain high performing staff.",""],[1,"31","2","Umwalimu SACCO Strengthening for Teacher Finance and Housing","Furthermore, Umwalimu SACCO will be strengthened to cater for teachers' access to affordable finance and housing.",""],[1,"31","3","SMART Classrooms and ICT Devices Scale-Up","Increase the use of ICT in teaching and learning through scaling up SMART classrooms and ICT devices as well as implementation of the new competence based curriculum.",""],[1,"31","4","Special Needs Education Support System","This will be achieved by developing a system for identifying children with special education needs, availing suitable special needs education materials, building capacity of teachers and ensuring accessibility of infrastructure such as inclusive sanitation facilities in order to create favorable learning environment.",""],[1,"31","7","Education Community Workers at Cell Level","This will be done through: (i) introducing Abajyanama b'Uburezi/Education community workers at Cell levels (Utugari).",""],[1,"31","7","School Data Management System Improvement","This will be done through: (ii) improving school data management system (SDMS) by introducing student identification numbers to track students' evolution and fight school dropouts,",""],[1,"31","7","School General Assembly Committee Parent Engagement","This will be done through: (iii) working with parents through School General Assembly Committees (SGACS).",""],[1,"42","5","Inclusive and Special Needs Education Workforce Development","Strengthening skills and increasing the number of professionals in inclusive and special needs education;",""],[1,"42","6","Assistive Devices and Learning Resources Expansion","Scaling up assistive devices and appropriate learning resources in education.",""],[1,"42","12","Village-Level Early Childhood Development Services Expansion","Scaling up ECDs services at village level;",""],[1,"49","5","Education System Improvement","To improve labor productivity, public expenditure will be directed towards improving the education system, supporting technological efforts to realize efficiency gains in land and agriculture, and enhancing the quality of infrastructure.",""],[1,"72","3","Standardized Early Childhood Education Schools Expansion","Promote standardized Early Childhood Education schools in all villages through partnership with private sector and local communities",""],[1,"72","3","School Infrastructure and Inclusive Sanitation Upgrade","Upgrade and increase school infrastructure and ensure access to adequate equipment & inclusive sanitation facilities",""],[1,"72","3","In-Service Teacher Training and Learner-Centered Pedagogy Programme","Scale up in-service education and learner-centered training,",""],[1,"72","3","Teacher Recruitment Incentives and Retention Support","Provide incentives to attract brilliant students to join the teaching profession and retain high performing staff.",""],[1,"72","3","Teacher Finance and Housing Support through Umwalimu Sacco","Strengthen Umwalimu Sacco to cater for teachers' access to affordable finance and housing.",""],[1,"72","3","SMART Classroom and ICT Device Expansion","Scale up SMART classrooms and ICT devices as well as use of the new competence based curriculum",""],[1,"72","3","Special Needs Education Identification and Support System","Develop a system to identify children with special education needs,",""],[1,"72","3","Special Needs Education Materials and Teacher Capacity Building","Avail suitable special needs education materials and build capacity of teachers",""],[1,"73","1","School Dropout Tracking and Community Support Mechanism","Introduce Abajyanama b'Uburezi at cell levels (Utugari) and improve school data management system (SDMS) by introducing student identification numbers to track students' evolution and fight school dropouts, · Work with parents through School General Assembly Committees (SGACs) to fight school dropouts.",""]],"34":[[1,"12","11","Malnutrition Prevention and Management Programme","Eradicate Malnutrition through enhanced prevention and management of all forms of malnutrition.",""],[1,"12","12","Health Care Service Improvement and Health Workforce Capacity Strengthening","Focus will be on improving health care services at all levels, strengthening financial sustainability of the health sector, and enhancing capacity of health workforce.",""],[1,"29","5","Maternal, Infant, and Child Health Improvement Efforts","Efforts will be intensified to improve maternal, infant, and child health and consequently reduce mortality in the respective categories.",""],[1,"29","6","Health Workforce Expansion","The number of active registered health workers will be quadrupled to improve the quality of healthcare and strengthen the prevention and treatment of communicable and non-communicable diseases.",""],[1,"29","7","Health Promotion and Disease Prevention Awareness Campaign","Awareness will be raised on positive behavior and lifestyle changes for disease prevention such as good nutrition practices, exercising and avoidance of behaviors that lead to alcoholism, drug abuse and teenage pregnancies, among others.",""],[1,"29","7","Mental Health Services Scale-Up","Mental health professionals and related services will be scaled up and strengthened.",""],[1,"30","1","Community Based Health Insurance Service Enhancement","The quality of Community Based Health Insurance (CBHI) services will be enhanced including review and expansion of the benefit package.",""],[1,"30","1","Community Health Worker Expansion and Professionalization","Community Health Workers (CHW) will be increased and their capacities will be enhanced with the aim of professionalizing them.",""]],"35":[[1,"12","10","Social Protection Programme Expansion and Scaling","Promote resilience to shocks and enhance Graduation from Poverty and extreme Poverty through improving and scaling up core and complementary social protection programs.",""],[1,"27","9","Support Programs for Vulnerable Groups","Enhance programs designed to support vulnerable groups to eradicate extreme poverty.",""],[1,"27","10","Minimum Package for Graduation Scale-Up","Scale up the minimum package for graduation (MPG);",""],[1,"27","10","Nationwide Roll-Out of VUP Expanded Public Works","prioritize nationwide roll-out of VUP expanded Public Works (with focus on female-headed households caring for young children)",""],[1,"27","10","Refocusing of VUP Classic Public Works to Shock-Prone Areas","and refocus VUP Classic Public Works to areas of the Country at most risk of seasonal and climate-related shocks.",""],[1,"27","11","One Cow per Poor Family (Girinka) Management Improvement","Improve the management of the One Cow per Poor Family (Girinka)",""],[1,"28","1","Girinka Program Guidelines Revision","This will be achieved through; revision of Girinka program guidelines, strengthening of pass on mechanism, development of a scalable model for acquisition and pass on of small livestock as well as finalization and operationalization of the Social Protection Management Information System (SPMIS).",""],[1,"28","1","Pass-On Mechanism Strengthening for Small Livestock Support","This will be achieved through; revision of Girinka program guidelines, strengthening of pass on mechanism, development of a scalable model for acquisition and pass on of small livestock as well as finalization and operationalization of the Social Protection Management Information System (SPMIS).",""],[1,"28","1","Scalable Small Livestock Acquisition and Pass-On Model","This will be achieved through; revision of Girinka program guidelines, strengthening of pass on mechanism, development of a scalable model for acquisition and pass on of small livestock as well as finalization and operationalization of the Social Protection Management Information System (SPMIS).",""],[1,"28","1","Social Protection Management Information System Operationalization","This will be achieved through; revision of Girinka program guidelines, strengthening of pass on mechanism, development of a scalable model for acquisition and pass on of small livestock as well as finalization and operationalization of the Social Protection Management Information System (SPMIS).",""],[1,"28","2","Household Profiling-Based Targeting for Poverty Eradication Programmes","Enhance targeting based on the nationwide roll-out of the household profiling",""],[1,"28","2","Multi-Stakeholder Coordination for Poverty Eradication Programmes","strengthen partnerships and coordination between government, non- governmental organizations (NGOs), Civil Society Organisations (CSOs), Faith-Based Organizations (FBOs), and the private sector in implementing poverty eradication programmes.",""],[1,"31","2","Household Poverty Graduation Support Interventions","This will be supported by interventions and innovations that promote people out of poverty and protect and prevent people from falling into poverty.",""],[1,"31","3","Multi-sectoral Poverty Graduation Support","Multi-sectoral interventions targeting vulnerable and poor populations will enable this, including providing access to technical, vocational and financial skills, productive assets (including toolkits and livestock) and complementary services such as business advisory, coaching and mentorship.",""],[1,"31","4","Expansion of Social Transfers for Poor and Vulnerable Populations","Protecting people who are in poverty without the capacity to graduate and preventing people from falling into poverty will be ensured through increasing coverage and adequacy of social transfers for poor and vulnerable populations.",""],[1,"31","4","Inclusive Social Security and Income Support Programs","This will be supported through inclusive social security and income support programs, such as Vision Umurenge Program (VUP) and Community Based Health Insurance (CBHI), as well as initiatives that encourage savings (including Ejo Heza) and insurance to protect households from shocks as well as reducing malnutrition through the provision of social transfers to pregnant women and children during the first 1000 days of life.",""],[1,"42","3","Disability Social Protection Scheme Expansion and Redesign","Scaling up coverage and re-designing social protection schemes to eligible People with Disabilities,",""],[1,"43","1","Street Children Reintegration and Delinquency Prevention Coordination","Enhancing coordination among stakeholders to reintegrate street children and prevent delinquency.",""],[1,"71","2","Minimum Package for Graduation Scale-Up","Scale up the minimum package for graduation (MPG);",""],[1,"71","2","Nationwide Expansion of VUP Expanded Public Works","Prioritize nationwide roll-out of VUP expanded Public Works (with focus on female-headed house- holds caring for young children)",""],[1,"71","2","Social Protection Programme Implementation Improvement","Review and improve implementation Social protection programmes to catalyze for rapid graduation",""],[1,"71","2","Climate-Shock-Responsive VUP Public Works Refocusing","Refocus VUP Classic Public Works to areas of the country at most risk of seasonal and climate- re- lated shocks",""],[1,"71","2","Girinka Guidelines Revision and Pass-On Mechanism Strengthening","Revise Girinka program guidelines and strengthen Girinka pass on mechanism,",""],[1,"71","2","Small Livestock Acquisition and Pass-On Model","Develop a scalable model for acquisition and pass on of small livestock as well as finalize and opera- tionalize the social protection Management Information System.",""],[1,"71","2","Household Profiling and Stakeholder Coordination for Targeting","Scale up household profiling in all ubudehe categories to inform targeting as well as strengthen partnerships and coordination among stakeholders including CSOs.",""]],"36":[[1,"32","2","Case Backlog Reduction in the Justice System","Reduce case backlogs in the justice system by half",""],[1,"32","5","Justice System Capacity Strengthening","the justice system's capacity will be strengthened, focusing on reducing the case backlogs by half and improving justice service delivery.",""],[1,"32","6","Alternative Dispute Resolution and Criminal Justice Reform","This will be delivered by enhancing the efficiency and effectiveness of existing Alternative Dispute Resolution (ADR) and Criminal Justice policies to increase cases settled through mediation and plea-bargaining.",""],[1,"32","6","Review and Update of Court Procedures and Laws","In addition, existing laws and court procedures will be reviewed and updated to increase the uptake of mediation and plea-bargaining including those relating to summary procedures and provisional detention.",""],[1,"32","7","Judiciary Career Development Policy","The career development policy in the judiciary will be implemented to further strengthen capacity and capabilities of judicial personnel.",""],[1,"32","7","Justice Service Delivery Modernization","Improving justice service delivery will also be achieved through the adoption of innovative technologies, enhancing the functioning and use of the Integrated Electronic Case Management System (IECMS), upgrading the Forensic Institute and making its services more accessible to the public.",""],[1,"36","6","Judiciary Reform to Reduce Case Backlog","Reform the Judiciary to tackle backlog cases, especially for Supreme Court with the aim of reducing the rate of backlog cases from 27.5% (2016 Supreme Court) to below 10% by 2024.",""],[1,"36","6","Unconventional Measures to Reduce Ombudsman Case Backlog","Unconventional methods will also be adopted to reduce backlog of cases at the Ombudsman.",""],[1,"36","7","Justice System Modernization and Electronic Case Management","Improve Access to quality justice by modernizing the Criminal, Commercial and Civil Justice System, enhancing professionalism in the judicial system and establishing specialized units in areas of criminal, commercial and civil justice system.",""],[1,"36","8","Legal Aid Provision Streamlining and Outreach Expansion","Legal Aid Provision will be streamlined to ensure Universal and affordable quality justice.",""],[1,"37","2","Alternative Dispute Resolution Strengthening","Enhance Alternative Dispute resolution mechanisms to promote the culture of problem-solving in families and reinforce amicable settlement of disputes.",""],[1,"37","2","Abunzi Management Information System","The Abunzi Management Information System will be put in place to facilitate data collection and sharing.",""],[1,"37","2","Sector-Level Abunzi Reinforcement","Activities of Abunzi at Sector level (Umurenge) will be reinforced.",""],[1,"75","2","Judicial Reform and Case Management Modernization","Reform the Judiciary to tackle backlog cases especially in the Supreme Court · Improve Access to quality justice by modernizing the Criminal, Commercial and Civil Justice System · Continue to professionalize the judicial system and establish specialized units in areas of criminal, commercial and civil justice. · Fully operationalize and rollout the Integrated Electronic case management system in all relevant institutions involved in case management.",""],[1,"75","2","Justice Outreach Expansion","Scale up MAJ outreach activities from Districts to Sector levels.",""],[1,"75","2","Alternative Dispute Resolution Strengthening","Enhance Alternative Dispute resolution mechanisms to promote the culture of problem-solving in families and reinforce amicable settlement of disputes",""],[1,"75","2","Abunzi Information System","Put in place Abunzi Management Information System",""]],"37":[[1,"32","8","Citizen Participation Platform and Feedback Mechanism Strengthening","This priority will be implemented by enhancing the efficiency and effectiveness of existing citizen participation platforms and strengthening feedback mechanisms to expedite citizens' problem-solving and improve accountability.",""],[1,"37","6","Citizen Accountability for NST2 Implementation","Provide accountability to citizens on implementation of NST2",""],[1,"38","9","Capacity Building for Civil Society and Private Sector Engagement","Build capacities of media, non-governmental organizations (NGOs), FBOs, and the private sector to effectively engage in and substantively contribute to national development, democratic governance and improving citizens' social welfare.",""],[1,"38","10","Decentralized Citizen Participation Mechanisms","Reinforce mechanisms at decentralized levels for citizens particularly women and youth to effectively contribute to districts planning and prioritization.",""],[1,"38","10","Online Platforms and Social Media for Citizen Engagement","Develop and utilize online platforms and social media to",""],[1,"42","11","Citizen Engagement in Development Programmes","Ensure and strengthen citizen engagement in :selected: development programmes",""],[1,"43","8","Civil Society Engagement and Accountability Strengthening","the role of civil society as a key implementing partner will be enhanced by promoting accountability, strengthening citizen engagement, and ensuring that development goals align with community needs",""],[1,"77","3","Capacity Building for Civil Society and Private Sector Engagement","Build capacities of media, non-governmental organizations (NGOs), CSOs, FBOs, and the private sector to effectively engage in and substantively contribute to national development",""],[1,"77","3","Decentralized Citizen Participation Mechanisms","Reinforce mechanisms at decentralized levels for citizens particularly women and youth to effectively contribute to districts planning and prioritization",""]],"38":[[1,"32","9","Institutional Governance Strengthening for Delivery","Institutional governance for delivery will be strengthened to accelerate and improve the implementation of development projects and programs and to provide quality services.",""],[1,"32","9","Regular Service Delivery Assessments","Service delivery in the public and private sector will be reinforced through carrying out regular assessments to identify gaps and recommend strategies for continuous improvement in quality of services.",""],[1,"32","10","Public Service Reform and Capacity Strengthening","This will entail reforming the public service in both central and local governments and strengthening their capacities.",""],[1,"32","10","Private Service Quality Improvement Sensitization","In addition, private service providers will be sensitized to strengthen the quality of services delivered to the community, such as hospitality, travel and tourism, financial services and others to leverage the vital contributions of the private sector to economic development.",""],[1,"43","6","Project Design Improvement","This includes strengthening cross-sectoral coordination, improving project design, and strengthening collaboration and engagement at all levels.",""],[1,"44","4","Outcome-Oriented Project Planning and Preparation","Project planning, design, and preparation will enhance the focus on outcomes rather than outputs to accelerate delivery.",""],[1,"67","2","Public Service Quality and Customer Care Improvement","Achieve high standards/ quality services and customer care across public and private sectors",""]],"39":[[1,"32","11","Public Financial Management Compliance and Anti-Corruption Strengthening","Efforts will be made to increase compliance with PFM rules and ensure value-for- money oversight.",""],[1,"32","13","Digital Transformation of IFMIS","This will involve the digital transformation of the Integrated Financial Management Information System (IFMIS) as a decision-making tool using artificial intelligence and big data analytics,",""],[1,"32","13","Expansion of E-Procurement Coverage","expanding the e-procurement (Umucyo) coverage,",""],[1,"32","13","Modernization of Revenue Collection Infrastructure","modernizing revenue collection infrastructure,",""],[1,"32","13","Digitization of Audit Processes","and digitizing audit processes.",""],[1,"32","13","Local Government Revenue Management System Enhancement","Local government revenue management systems will also be enhanced to support better resource mobilization.",""],[1,"33","1","Climate-Responsive Public Financial Management Enhancement","climate-responsive PFM will be enhanced by integrating sustainability into public investment management and supporting green procurement.",""],[1,"33","1","PFM Staff Climate Risk Management and Reporting Capacity Building","PFM staff will be equipped to manage climate- related risks and report on them effectively.",""]],"40":[[1,"33","4","Civic Education Cultural Values Institutionalization","National unity, resilience and civic engagement will be strengthened by continuing to institutionalize Rwandan culture and values in civic education (Ndi Umunyarwanda, Itorero, etc.) and national development programs.",""],[1,"33","5","Genocide Ideology Prevention and Anti-Discrimination Education Campaign","The prevention and fight against genocide ideology and all forms of discrimination will be reinforced.",""],[1,"34","12","Kinyarwanda and Civic Values Promotion through Itorero","Enshrine Kinyarwanda language and Rwandan values of integrity, transparency, fighting injustice and intolerance for corruption among Rwandans in families, schools' curricula and the youth.",""],[1,"35","1","Establishment of the National Itorero Education Center and Provincial Branches","Education Center for the \"Itorero ry'lgihugu\" and one branch per Province will be established to foster a mindset that accelerates development and national self-reliance.",""],[1,"35","2","Institutionalization of Unity and Reconciliation Programmes","Promote unity andreconciliation among Rwandans through Institutionalization of \"Ndi Umunyarwanda and Abarinzi b'Igihango\" programmes in Local government and scale up of unity clubs to village level.",""],[1,"37","4","Genocide Ideology Prevention and Prosecution Cooperation","This will be achieved by enhancing regional and international cooperation in Genocide ideology prevention and prosecution.",""],[1,"37","4","Genocide Evidence Conservation and Preservation","Also conservation and preservation of proofs of the Genocide against Tutsi will be reinforced.",""],[1,"39","2","Home-Grown Solutions Development Initiative","develop Home-Grown Solutions to problems encountered by different categories of our society;",""],[1,"39","2","Strengthening of the Voluntary National Service Program","Strengthen the voluntary national service program (Urugerero) under the national civic education institution (Itorero ry'lgihugu) with the objective of developing the Rwandan youth into citizens who aspire to become self-reliant and hardworking.",""],[1,"39","3","Home Grown Solutions Center of Excellence","Establish and fully operationalize Home Grown Solutions Center of Excellence to preserve and promote productive cultural heritage and innovations that constitute drivers of recovery and development for post-genocide Rwanda.",""],[1,"39","3","Documentation of Rwanda's Transformational Leadership Legacy","Document the legacies, impacts and trends of Rwanda's transformational leadership in social, economic and political spheres and make them available for lessons and use by future generations, Africa and the Global Community.",""],[1,"74","2","National Civic Education Center and Provincial Branches","Establish a model National Civic Education Center for the \"Itorero ry'lgihugu\" and one branch per Province to foster a mindset that accelerates development and national self-reliance.",""],[1,"74","2","Nationwide Itorero Operationalization","Operationalize Itorero in all villages and schools.",""],[1,"74","2","Institutionalization of Ndi Umunyarwanda and Abarinzi b'Igihango Programmes","Institutionalize \"Ndi Umunyarwanda and Abarinzi b'Igihango\" programmes in Local government and scale up unity clubs to village level",""],[1,"75","2","Anti-Genocide Ideology Campaign","Intensify fight against genocide ideology in Rwanda and anywhere in the world",""],[1,"77","3","Home-Grown Solutions and Innovation Promotion","Consolidate and develop home-grown solutions and innovations",""],[1,"77","3","Home Grown Solutions Center of Excellence","Establish and fully operationalize Home Grown Solutions Center of Excellence",""]],"41":[[1,"33","6","Professionalization and Capacity Enhancement of Security Organs","Crime prevention and response, public order, safety, security, and territorial integrity will be sustained and strengthened by continuing to professionalize and enhance the capacity of security organs while continuously engaging and working with communities to contribute to Rwanda's socio-economic development.",""],[1,"33","6","Community Engagement for Crime Prevention and Public Safety","Crime prevention and response, public order, safety, security, and territorial integrity will be sustained and strengthened by continuing to professionalize and enhance the capacity of security organs while continuously engaging and working with communities to contribute to Rwanda's socio-economic development.",""],[1,"33","6","Bilateral and Multilateral Peace and Security Cooperation","Rwanda will also continue contributing to peace and security through bilateral, regional and international cooperation.",""],[1,"34","8","Security Institutions Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen capacity of security institutions/organs to preserve national security and protect Rwandans, as well as actively participate in socio- economic development of the Nation.",""],[1,"35","5","Community Policing for Crime Prevention","Strengthen Crime prevention through community policing working with citizens.",""],[1,"35","6","Security Organs Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen capacity of all security organs (Armed Forces, Police, security companies and NISS) for effective discharge of their functions.",""],[1,"35","7","Regional and International Security Partnership Expansion","Enhance and expand regional and international security partnerships to fight and prevent cross-border crimes, human and drug trafficking and cybercrimes;",""],[1,"36","3","Rwandan Peacekeepers Excellence and Humanitarian Capacity Maintenance","Continue contributing to peace and security in Africa and globally while ensuring that Rwandan Peacekeepers maintain a culture of excellence in humanitarian and peacekeeping activities.",""],[1,"74","5","Community Policing Crime Prevention","Strengthen Crime prevention through community policing working with citizens",""],[1,"74","5","Security Organs Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen capacity of all security organs (Armed Forces, Police, security companies and NISS) for effective discharge of their functions",""],[1,"74","5","Regional and International Security Partnerships","Expand regional and international security partnerships to fight and prevent cross-border crimes, human and drug trafficking and cybercrimes",""]],"42":[[1,"34","6","Legal Frameworks for Economic Development and Institutional Accountability","Establish legal frameworks that spur economic development and instill fairness, transparency and accountability across institutions and individuals,",""],[1,"37","1","Legal Review, Revision, and Translation Programme","Draft, revise and modernize Laws taking into account Rwanda's cultural context.",""],[1,"37","3","Anti-Corruption Enforcement and Whistleblower Protection Measures","Efforts to prevent and fight corruption will be intensified.",""],[1,"75","2","Legal Drafting and Law Modernization","Draft, revise and modernize Laws taking into account Rwanda's cultural context",""],[1,"75","2","Whistleblower Protection and Incentive Scheme","Strengthen the protection of whistle-blowers and implement internal incentive scheme for whistle blowers",""],[1,"75","2","Anti-Corruption Investigation Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen the capacity of the Office of the Ombudsman and RIB to investigate corruption related cases","Office of the Ombudsman | RIB"]],"43":[[1,"19","2","Kigali Innovation City Skills Ecosystem Development","Develop and operationalize a thriving skills ecosystem for attracting and nurturing local and international talent around the Kigali Innovation City (KIC) model.",""],[1,"19","3","Innovation Fund for Firms in the Innovation and Technology Industry","Operationalize the innovation fund to support firms in the innovation and technology industry.",""],[1,"19","6","Research and Development Promotion for Industrial Technology","Promote research and development as a key to fast-tracking Rwanda's economic transformation especially in the area of technology for industrial development.",""],[1,"20","2","Kigali Innovation City ICT Services Support","Interventions will include: leveraging Kigali Innovation City as a mechanism to spur ICT services including BPOs,",""],[1,"21","11","Research and Innovation Strengthening Initiative","The impact of research and innovation will be strengthened to enhance competitiveness and expand market access.",""],[1,"21","11","Progressive R&D Spending Increase with Private Sector Partnership","Spending on research and development (R&D) will be progressively increased in partnership with the private sector.",""]],"44":[[1,"29","6","Pharmaceutical and Medical Equipment Industry Promotion","Promote industries in pharmaceuticals and manufacturing of medical equipment as well as support medical research.",""],[1,"72","1","Pharmaceutical and Medical Equipment Industry Promotion","Promote industries in pharmaceuticals and manufacturing of medical equipment as well as support medical research",""]],"45":[[1,"14","3","National Strategy for Transformation (NST1)","The implementation instrument for the remainder of Vision 2020 and for the first four years of the journey under Vision 2050 will be the National Strategy for Transformation (NST1).",""],[1,"36","3","Strategic Implementation Review and Corrective Action Mechanism","Receive strategic level reports on implementation :selected: performance and take high level decisions on corrective actions needed",""],[1,"37","3","Annual Leadership-Level Strategic Reviews","Conduct annual leadership-level reviews of strategic areas of the NST-2.",""],[1,"38","4","Technical-Level Implementation Challenge Resolution","Identify and unblock implementation challenges at technical level.",""],[1,"42","3","Evaluation, Research and Studies Coordination for NST2 Implementation","Coordinate evaluations, research and studies to :selected: support lesson learning in the implementation of NST2",""],[1,"44","2","Strengthened Monitoring and Evaluation","Additional emphasis will be put on strengthening monitoring and evaluation.",""],[1,"54","7","Results-Based Management Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","The monitoring and evaluation functions shall follow the guidelines stipulated in the Results Based Management (RBM) policy which provides for the M&E frequency as well as roles and responsibilities for each stakeholder.",""],[1,"55","6","NST1 Implementation Monitoring and Acceleration Measures","Monitor the implementation of NST1, propose measures to fast track its implementation.",""],[1,"55","9","NST1 Implementation Monitoring and Strategic Guidance","Monitor implementation of NST1 in different clusters · Provide strategic guidance and orientation on policies and · investments to deliver on NST1.",""],[1,"55","14","National Monitoring and Evaluation Coordination and Reporting System","Overall coordination of M&E activities from planning, data collection, and reporting at all levels",""],[1,"55","14","NST Consolidated Annual Reporting","Prepare the NST consolidated annual report using the reports from different sectors",""],[1,"55","14","Government Command Centre KPI Monitoring","Monitor the macro KPIs through the Government Command Centre (GCC)",""],[1,"55","14","Annual Budget and Public Investment Alignment Mechanism","Ensure the alignment between annual budget planning and · Public Investment Committee projects with priority areas outlined in NST1",""],[1,"56","1","NST1 Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","The role of the Monitoring and Evaluation (M&E) framework is to track, update and report on the progress and impact of interventions outlined under NST1 as well as ensuring that information, data and analysis are of the best quality.",""],[1,"56","2","National Results-Based Management Policy and NST1 M&E Framework","The National Results Based Management (RBM) Policy provides the guidance for the design and structuring of the NST1 M&E framework.",""],[1,"56","2","ICT-Enabled Monitoring and Evaluation System","M&E will leverage ICT tools and innovations to support timely and effective update of the performance information.",""],[1,"56","7","ICT-Based Monitoring and Data Collection Enhancement","NST1 M&E activities will build on existing ICT based monitoring tools (such as IFMIS, Imihigo Dashboard and sectoral MIS).",""],[1,"57","1","Primary Data Collection Enhancement","applications will be encouraged to enhance collection of primary data.",""],[1,"57","5","Disaggregated Monitoring and Results-Based Evaluation System","During the monitoring and reporting of NST1 implementation, key disaggregation of data will be encouraged.",""],[1,"57","6","Evaluation Activities and Joint Sector Reviews","Evaluation activities will be carried out at national, sectoral and district levels.",""],[1,"57","7","NST1 Mid-term Evaluation","A national level mid-term evaluation for NST1 will be conducted to provide the status and proposals to fast track progress.",""]],"46":[[1,"33","2","High-Quality and Timely Data for Evidence-Based Decision-Making","Lastly, generating high-quality and timely data will support evidence-based decision-making in planning, budgeting, monitoring and evaluation.",""]],"47":[[1,"12","5","Agricultural Productivity and Climate-Resilient Farming Support","Achieving this growth will require improvements in agricultural productivity by optimizing land use, enhancing yields of priority food crops and adopting efficient and climate-resilient farming practices.",""],[1,"12","5","Farmer Access to Inputs, Extension, Finance, and Markets","Additionally, farmers will need greater access to modern agriculture inputs, extension services, financing and markets to scale up their operations.",""]],"48":[[1,"13","2","Foreign Exchange Rate Policy for Export Promotion","a suitable foreign exchange-rate policy will be adopted to promote exports and enhance international competitiveness.",""]],"49":[[1,"17","4","Regenerative Conservation Agriculture Promotion","Regenerative conservation agriculture practices will be further promoted to protect land health and maintain land productivity and agro-ecology.",""]],"50":[[1,"18","1","Private Investment Attraction for Priority Manufacturing Sub-Sectors","This strategy will be anchored in attracting private investment in priority manufacturing sub-sectors such as agro-processing, horticulture, mineral processing, leather, automotive, creative industries, biomanufacturing, pharmaceuticals, textiles and apparel.",""]],"51":[[1,"18","2","Green and Clean Technology Adoption in Priority Industries","The adoption of modern green and clean technologies in priority industries will be promoted to further develop sustainable industries.",""]],"52":[[1,"18","5","Mineral Exploration and Mining Sector Professionalization Programme","The growth in the mining sector will be led by a combination of mineral exploration, professionalization of artisanal miners, adoption of environmentally friendly mining practices as well as enhanced processing and value addition of key minerals.",""],[1,"18","5","Environmentally Friendly Mining Practices","The growth in the mining sector will be led by a combination of mineral exploration, professionalization of artisanal miners, adoption of environmentally friendly mining practices as well as enhanced processing and value addition of key minerals.",""],[1,"18","5","Mineral Processing and Value Addition Initiative","The growth in the mining sector will be led by a combination of mineral exploration, professionalization of artisanal miners, adoption of environmentally friendly mining practices as well as enhanced processing and value addition of key minerals.",""],[1,"18","5","Traditional Export Value Addition Scale-Up","Traditional exports (coffee, tea, pyrethrum,) will also continue to be scaled up with an emphasis on value addition across value chains.",""]],"53":[[1,"20","2","Public Transport Infrastructure and Service Upgrade","Public transport infrastructure and services will be upgraded to support economic development.",""]],"54":[[1,"20","7","Strategic Port Construction and Operation","Maritime transportand trade across Lake Kivuwill be improved by constructing and operationalizing strategic ports in Rusizi, Karongi and Rutsiro(Nkora) in partnership with the private sector.",""],[1,"20","7","One-Stop Border Post Development and Operationalization","Developing and operationalizing One- Stop Border Posts (OSBP) remains a key priority to enhance regional transport connectivity and facilitate trade with neighboring countries.",""],[1,"35","1","Cross-Border Trade Facilitation and Non-Tariff Barrier Reduction","the Government of Rwanda will continue to expand cross-border trade and eliminate non-tariff barriers including improving trade logistic infrastructure and harmonizing regulatory frameworks across the region.",""],[1,"35","1","Joint Regional Infrastructure Project Advocacy","Key strategic interventions will involve advocating for the implementation of joint infrastructure projects critical to regional integration",""],[1,"35","1","Broadband Expansion and Regional Transport Corridor Upgrading","as well as extending the geographic reach of broadband infrastructure, and enhancing regional transport corridors to reduce trade costs, improve connectivity, and bolster Rwanda's integration into regional and global markets.",""]],"55":[[1,"21","2","Flagship Projects for Urban Economic Development","Economic activities in CoK, satellite and secondary cities and other urban areas will be enhanced by implementing flagship projects that leverage local economic potentials.",""],[1,"21","2","Backward and Forward Linkage Development","This will be complemented by harnessing backward and forward linkages and opportunities linked to major investments in agro- processing, infrastructure, tourism, sports and entertainment, entrepreneurship and innovation hubs, among others.",""]],"56":[[1,"21","3","Urban Wetland Rehabilitation and Green Open Space Expansion","rehabilitation of urban wetlands will be undertaken and green open spaces developed and scaled up.",""]],"57":[[1,"22","5","National Savings Mobilization and Alternative Financing Expansion","Achieving this target will require expanding traditional financial channels and diversifying and mobilizing alternative funding sources to meet the growing demand for investment.",""],[1,"22","6","Alternative Financing Mobilization for Emerging Businesses","a concerted effort will be made to attract innovative financing such as blended financing, venture capital, and crowdfunding among others.",""],[1,"23","2","Collective Investment Scheme Product Diversification","diversify the number of Collective Investment Scheme products available to investors, offering a broader range of investment options to encourage participation in the financial market.",""],[1,"23","3","Capital Market Strengthening and Integration Reform","capital markets will be strengthened to improve access to capital for businesses by establishing robust regulatory and governance frameworks that enhance transparency and investor protection to build market confidence, investing in modern trading and settlement infrastructure to streamline operations and reduce transaction costs.",""],[1,"23","3","Innovative Financial Instruments and Services Initiative","This will be complemented by introducing innovative financial instruments and services and facilitating cross-border investments through regional capital market integration.",""],[1,"23","3","Investment Clinic Programme Enhancement","the investment clinic program, which assists companies, particularly SMEs, in becoming 'listing-ready' will also be enhanced.",""],[1,"23","5","Fintech Startup Growth and Digital Innovation Market Infrastructure","To foster innovation, there will be a focus on promoting the growth of Fintech startups and developing effective market infrastructure that supports investments in digital innovations.",""],[1,"23","5","Financial System Strengthening and Investor Attraction Initiative","Rwanda aims to position itself as a leading international financial hub by strengthening its financial systems and attracting high-value investors and financial actors to the financial center.",""],[1,"23","6","Introduction of New and Alternative Capital and Financial Services","steps will be taken to facilitate the introduction of new and alternative forms of capital, including innovative financial products and services, private banking, and wealth management to broaden the offerings within the financial center.",""],[1,"23","6","Central Bank Digital Currency Scoping Initiative","The National Bank of Rwanda (NBR) is scoping the introduction of a Central Bank Digital Currency (CBDC) to drive innovation, support the shift to a cashless economy, and improve cross-border transaction efficiency.","National Bank of Rwanda (NBR)"]],"58":[[1,"27","9","Dropout Reduction Efforts","Strengthening efforts to curb and reduce drop-outs",""],[1,"27","11","Pre-Primary Education Expansion Programme","Pre-primary education will prioritize increasing net enrollment from 35% to 65% by developing infrastructure, increasing the number of trained teachers, and providing essential teaching and learning materials.",""]],"59":[[1,"30","3","Drug Discovery and Pharmaceutical Manufacturing Promotion","Additionally, efforts will be put into promoting drug discovery research and attracting investment in local manufacturing of pharmaceuticals.",""]],"60":[[1,"31","5","Civil Society Alignment with Social Protection Frameworks","Civil Society Organizations will be encouraged and required to align their interventions with national Social Protection policies, strategies and guidelines in order to make the most effective use of available funding.",""],[1,"31","6","Strengthened Coordination and Monitoring Framework for Social Protection","the coordination and monitoring framework will be strengthened among Government Institutions, Development Partners, Civil Society Organizations, the Private Sector and Faith-Based Organizations through joint planning and monitoring efforts.",""]],"61":[[1,"33","3","Economic Diplomacy and Trade Promotion Initiative","International cooperation and diplomacy will be strengthened to accelerate Rwanda's economic development with a focus on economic diplomacy.",""],[1,"33","3","Trade, Investment, and Tourism Promotion through AfCFTA","This includes securing trade and investment opportunities and boosting tourism by leveraging initiatives such as the African Continental Free Trade Area (AfCFTA) agreement.",""],[1,"33","3","Rwandan Diaspora Engagement and Service Improvement","The Rwandan Community Abroad will be mobilized and engaged to sustain participation in the national development agenda and the quality of services rendered to them will be improved.",""],[1,"34","12","Trade and Investment Agreement Implementation","This will be done through implementing initiatives such as the African Continental Free Trade Area (AfCFTA), preferential trade agreements, bilateral trade and investment treaties, double taxation agreements among others.",""]],"62":[[1,"34","4","Disability and Social Inclusion Mainstreaming and Capacity-Building","One of the key focus areas will include increasing the level of citizen participation and inclusiveness by ensuring that persons with Disabilities, their organizations, and other vulnerable groups are capacitated to play an active role in the transformational programs.",""]],"63":[[1,"34","6","Targeted HIV/AIDS Awareness Campaigns for Youth and AGYW","Targeted awareness campaigns for youth, especially Adolescent Girls and Young Women (AGYW), will be conducted",""],[1,"34","6","Voluntary Medical Male Circumcision Prevention Intervention","alongside promoting effective prevention interventions for men, including voluntary Medical Male Circumcision",""],[1,"34","6","Comprehensive HIV/AIDS Policy Development and Implementation","Comprehensive policies will be developed and implemented in collaboration with multiple stakeholders to address HIV/ AIDS, reduce stigma and discrimination, improve the socio-economic status of affected populations, and human rights, reduce inequalities and gender- based violence, and ensure social and legal protection for those living with or affected by HIV/AIDS.",""]],"64":[[1,"34","7","NCD Prevention Public Awareness Campaigns","the government will promote a whole-of-society, life-course and multisectoral collaboration approach, for a sustainable response.",""],[1,"34","7","Community Health Worker NCD Prevention and Screening Capacity Building","capacity-building initiatives for community health workers and certified public health workers on NCDs prevention and early detection/screening to enable them to drive community NCDs awareness programs.",""]],"65":[[1,"34","8","Gender Equality in Access to Productive Resources","The focus will be on ensuring equal access, use, and control over productive resources by men and women both in urban and rural areas to support inclusive accelerated economic growth,",""],[1,"34","8","Women's Technical Skills Development in Male-Dominated Sectors","developing women's technical skills in male- dominated areas such as infrastructure, industry, mining, Agri-Hub, sports, and creative industry to support their entrepreneurship, employability, business development, and trade opportunities.",""],[1,"34","8","Gender Mainstreaming in Education and ICT-STEM-TVET","efforts will be made to further institutionalize gender equality in all levels of education, including bridging the gender divide in ICT, STEM, and TVET education programs as well",""]],"66":[[1,"69","2","Cultural and Creative Industry Ecosystem Strengthening","PA-9. Strengthen and promote the cultural and creative industry Ecosystem",""],[1,"70","2","Arts Centers and Facilities Development","Develop and establish arts centers/Facility in CoK and secondary cities",""]],"67":[[1,"18","5","Flagship Projects in Secondary Cities and Key Urban Areas","7. Develop Flagship projects in secondary cities and other key urban areas to support thriving and sustainable urban economies (with employment and incomes).",""],[1,"18","6","Update and Implement Urban Master Plans","Update Master plans of secondary cities and other key towns to reflect the ambition to become modern cities and towns.",""],[1,"18","9","Basic Infrastructure Development for Residential Zones and Urban Roads","Develop Basic infrastructure through servicing 250 km of new residential zones and upgrading 288 km of unpaved urban roads.",""],[1,"18","9","Public Lighting Installation on Major Roads","Public lighting will also be installed on major national and district roads.",""]],"68":[[1,"13","6","Diplomatic and International Cooperation Strengthening","Strengthen Diplomatic and International Cooperation to Accelerate Rwanda and Africa's Development.",""],[1,"13","8","Public Institutions Capacity, Service Delivery and Accountability Strengthening","· Strengthen Capacity, Service Delivery and Accountability of Public Institutions.",""],[1,"15","3","Home-Grown Solutions Scaling Initiative","Adopting and scaling up Home-Grown Solutions based on Rwandan culture, values and the country's unique developmental context",""]],"69":[[1,"11","3","Climate-Resilient Farming and Value Chain Investment","investments in climate resilient techniques for farming coupled with improvements in value chains is expected to yield significant future gains in both growth and poverty reduction.",""],[1,"12","7","Agriculture and Livestock Modernization and Productivity Improvement","Modernize and increase the productivity of agriculture and livestock.",""],[1,"17","6","Agriculture and Livestock Productivity Improvement","· Increase agriculture and livestock quality, productivity and production",""],[1,"22","6","Agricultural Export Crop Productivity Expansion","Growth of Agricultural exports will be complemented by increasing the volume of traditional agriculture export crops and products.",""]],"70":[[1,"22","3","Mining Exploration and Export Expansion Programme","Upscale mining by completing exploration of potential mineral areas to establish the extent of national resources and reserves, in terms of quantity and quality with the aim of exporting USD 800 million by 2020 and USD 1.5 billion annually by 2024 from USD 373 million in 2017.",""],[1,"22","4","Artisanal Mining Professionalization Support Programme","The artisanal mining sector will be professionalized through training, financing and equipment.",""]],"71":[[1,"26","4","Water Flow Management Project","Develop a project to manage water flows from the volcano region and other rivers to mitigate related disasters and improve water resource management.",""],[1,"26","5","Land Administration and Management Reform","Strengthen land administration and management to ensure optimal allocation and use of land.",""],[1,"70","5","Volcano Region Water Flow Management Project","Develop a project to manage water flows from the volcano region and other rivers to mitigate relat- ed disasters and improve water resource management",""],[1,"70","5","Water Catchment Protection and Community Disaster Mitigation","Manage and protect water catchments to mitigate disasters in partnership with local communities.",""],[1,"70","5","Land Administration and Management Strengthening","Strengthen land administration and management to ensure optimal allocation and use of land",""]],"72":[[1,"29","4","Model Health Centers of Excellence for NCD Treatment","Establish model health centers of excellence through partnership with private investors for treatment of Non Communicable Diseases (NCDs) that normally require treatment abroad such as cancer, cardiac surgery, and complex trauma among others.",""],[1,"29","5","Innovative Health Sector Financing Mechanisms","Identify innovative sources of financing for the health sector including Public Private Partnerships, Public Community Partnership for health financing and sustainable model for Community Based Health Insurance (CBHI).",""],[1,"29","7","Disease Prevention Awareness Campaign","Strengthen disease prevention awareness and reduce Communicable and",""],[1,"30","2","Drug Abuse and Trafficking Sensitization Campaigns","Prevent and fight drug abuse and trafficking among all sections of the population especially youth through sensitization campaigns in partnership with stakeholders.",""],[1,"30","3","Reproductive Health and Family Planning Awareness and Access Expansion","Scale up efforts to raise awareness on reproductive health and family planning to increase contraceptive prevalence from 48% (2013/14) to 60% in 2024.",""],[1,"42","1","Specialized NCD Treatment Capacity Expansion","ii) scaling up specialized treatment options including building capacity at different levels of health care and medical personnel",""],[1,"42","1","Health Insurance Coverage Expansion for NCDs","iii) working with health insurance schemes to expand coverage of NCDs in packages offered to address the issue of affordability.",""],[1,"72","1","Model Health Centers of Excellence for NCD Treatment","Establish model health centers of excellence through partnership with private investors for treatment of Non Communicable Diseases (NCDs)",""],[1,"72","1","Innovative Health Sector Financing","Identify innovative sources of financing for the health sector",""],[1,"72","1","Disease Prevention Awareness Campaign","Strengthen disease prevention awareness and reduce Communicable and Non Communicable Diseases (NCDs)",""],[1,"72","1","Drug Abuse and Trafficking Prevention Initiative","Prevent and fight drug abuse and trafficking among all sections of the population especially youth",""],[1,"72","1","Reproductive Health and Family Planning Awareness Scale-Up","Scale up efforts to raise awareness on reproductive health and family planning to increase contraceptive prevalence",""]],"73":[[1,"33","4","Gender-Based Violence and Child Abuse Prevention and Response Strategy","Strengthen prevention and response strategies to fight gender-based violence (GBV) and child abuse.",""],[1,"33","4","Family Cohesion Home-Grown Initiatives","Specific interventions will include; establishing and strengthening family cohesion home grown initiatives",""],[1,"33","4","Integrated Health Care Services for GBV Victims","implementing the integrated health care services for GBV victims.",""],[1,"33","4","Community Awareness Campaigns on GBV and Child Abuse","partnerships will be strengthened with the Private sector, CSOs, Faith Based Organizations as well to conduct community awareness campaigns for fighting GBV and child abuse.",""],[1,"42","13","Gender-Based Violence and Human Trafficking Awareness and Prevention","Continuing awareness and fight against gender based violence and human trafficking;",""],[1,"73","3","Integrated Health Care Services for GBV Victims","Continue to implement the integrated health care services for GBV victims",""],[1,"73","3","Family Cohesion Home-Grown Initiatives","Establish new and strengthen existing family cohesion home grown initiatives such as Umugoroba w'Ababyeyi",""]],"74":[[1,"33","5","Orphan Family Reintegration and Follow-up Programme","Ensure that orphans are raised in families through; conducting awareness campaigns on \"Tubarere Mu Muryango\" program, reintegrating and following up reintegrated children as well as building the capacity of family protection volunteers/ Inshuti z'Umuryango.",""],[1,"42","4","Building Code Enforcement for Infrastructure Access","Ensuring easy access to public and private infrastructure by enforcing the building code;",""],[1,"42","10","Women’s Access to Finance Facilitation","Continuing to facilitate women to access finance;",""],[1,"42","11","Gender Mainstreaming in Employment and Job Creation Strategies","Mainstreaming gender in employment and job creation strategies;",""],[1,"73","3","Tubarere Mu Muryango Awareness Campaigns","Conduct awareness campaigns on \"Tubarere Mu Muryango\" program to ensure that orphans are raised in families",""],[1,"74","2","Gender Equality and Equal Opportunity Promotion","Promote gender equality and ensure equal opportunities for all Rwandans",""]],"75":[[1,"34","7","Economic Diplomacy and Regional Cooperation Foreign Policy","Strengthen foreign policy that is driven by economic diplomacy, regional cooperation/Integration and Pan Africanism,",""],[1,"35","9","Diplomacy and International Cooperation Strengthening","Strengthen diplomacy and international cooperation to support the promotion",""],[1,"36","1","Opening New Embassies and Commercial Attaché Coordination","This will be achieved through opening of new embassies and coordination of commercial attaches to attract potential investors in priority sectors to Rwanda.",""],[1,"36","1","Removal of Intra-African Trade Barriers","Rwanda will also advocate for continued removal of barriers to intra-African trade such as visa requirements and other obstacles to free movement of people and goods within the continent.",""],[1,"36","2","Pan-African Cooperation and AU Reform Support","Strive for unity of Africans and development of the continent based on cooperation and trade aimed at positioning Africa internationally and increasing its self-reliance; this will include promoting the spirit of Pan-Africanism and following through on the initiated reforms for the sustainability of the AU.",""],[1,"36","4","Diaspora Services Expansion and Engagement Programme","Expand services delivered to the diaspora community and sensitize the Rwandan diaspora to promote unity and reconciliation, increase participation in national development programs, and mobilize friends of Rwanda.",""],[1,"36","5","Home-Grown Solutions Awareness Mechanism","Put in place mechanisms to raise awareness of Rwanda's Home-Grown Solutions locally and internationally to support development.",""],[1,"43","5","Non-Tariff Barrier Elimination Advocacy","Promoting intra Africa and global trade through continued advocacy to eliminate Non-Tariff Barriers (NTB); and",""],[1,"74","8","New Embassy and Commercial Attaché Coordination Initiative","Open new embassies and enhance coordination of commercial attachés to attract potential investors in priority sectors to Rwanda.",""],[1,"74","8","Intra-African Trade Barrier Removal Advocacy","Advocate for continued removal of barriers to intra-Africa trade such as visa requirements and other obstacles to free movement of people and goods within the continent",""],[1,"74","8","Diaspora Services Expansion and Outreach","Expand services delivered to the diaspora community and sensitize the Rwandan diaspora",""],[1,"74","8","Home-Grown Solutions Awareness Mechanism","Put in place mechanisms to raise awareness of Rwanda's Home-Grown Solutions locally and internationally to support development",""]],"76":[[1,"35","3","Gender Mainstreaming Across Sectors and District Strategies","this will be achieved through mainstreaming gender across sectors, district strategies and investments.",""],[1,"42","11","Strengthening Gender Machinery and Mainstreaming Tools","Strengthening capacities of gender machinery and use of gender mainstreaming tools and disaggregated data to inform policy formulation and resource allocation;",""]],"77":[[1,"38","4","Public Project Appraisal and Feasibility Study Requirement","All public projects funded for implementation to be appraised by the Public Investment Committee as provided by the National Investment Policy to assure their quality and desired impact.",""],[1,"38","5","Coordination Strengthening for Clusters, Sector Working Groups, and JADF","Strengthen the functioning of clusters, sector working groups and JADF to enhance coordination in planning and implementation.",""],[1,"54","1","NST1 Oversight and Coordination Arrangements","The oversight function for implementing NST1 lies with the Parliament and Cabinet.",""],[1,"54","2","Oversight Support through National Coordination Fora","The oversight function will also be supported by different structures and fora that include National Umushyikirano Council, the National Leadership Retreat, Ministerial Cluster meetings among others.",""],[1,"54","3","Technical Coordination through the Permanent Secretary's Forum and Development Partners Coordination Group","Technical coordination will be undertaken through the Permanent Secretary's Forum and the Development Partners Coordination Group (DPCG),",""],[1,"54","4","Joint Sector Reviews for Sector Plan and Investment Follow-up","Sector Working groups (which bring together Government, Development partners, Private sector and civil society) will also follow up implementation of sectoral plans and investments through Joint Sector Reviews.",""],[1,"54","4","District Joint Actions Development Forum","At the district level, the Joint Actions Development Forum will bring together all stakeholders contributing to the delivery of the NST1 implemented through District Development Strategies.",""],[1,"54","5","National Development Planning and Budgeting Coordination","MINECOFIN will lead the national development planning and delivery process through coordinating the national planning and budgeting functions to ensure sectors and districts' plans are aligned to NST1 priorities.","MINECOFIN"],[1,"54","6","Coordination and Follow-up on District Development Strategy Implementation","MINALOC will support in the coordination and follow up on implementation of District Development Strategies.","MINALOC"],[1,"54","7","NST1 Delivery through Annual Plans, Budgets, and Imihigo","The delivery of NST1 will be undertaken through annual plans, budgets and imihigo (performance contracts).",""],[1,"55","2","Government Programme Coordination and Performance Monitoring","· Coordinate government activities/programmes · Monitor performance of the Government institutions both at central and local levels.",""],[1,"55","2","Joint Imihigo Cluster Coordination","· Coordinate clusters and implementation of Joint Imihigo",""],[1,"55","11","Sector Stakeholder Dialogue and Joint Review Mechanism","Provide a forum for dialogue, ownership and accountability of the development agenda by all stakeholders at sector level · Build synergies in policy formulation, implementation and enhance regular reviews · Conduct joint sector reviews (Forward and Backward reviews) · Monitor progress of the Sector Strategic Plan (SSP).",""],[1,"55","13","District-Level NST1 Coordination and Monitoring","Participate in the elaboration and implementation of imihigo · Monitor the implementation of District Development Strategies (DDSs) · Promote cooperation between the public sector, Private sector · and civil society to deliver on NST1 at district level",""],[1,"55","15","Coordination of District Development Strategy Implementation","Coordinate the implementation of Districts Development Strategies (DDSs)",""],[1,"55","15","Alignment of District Development Strategies with District Imihigo","Ensure the alignment between DDSs and Districts Imihigo",""],[1,"55","15","District Contribution to NST1 Targets","their contribution to NST1 targets",""],[1,"76","2","Public Investment Appraisal and Approval Mechanism","Implement the National Investment Policy by ensuring that all public funded projects are appraised by the Public Investment committee on the Central Government level and Projects Advisory Committee on the Local Government level",""],[1,"76","2","Planning and Implementation Coordination Strengthening","Strengthen the functioning of clusters, sector working groups and JADF to enhance coordination in planning and implementation",""]],"78":[[1,"43","8","Cross-Sectoral Coordination for Environmental Policy Implementation","Focus will be on improving cross sectoral coordination to ensure smooth implementation of environmental policies and regulations.",""],[1,"44","2","Environmental and Social Impact Assessments","High impact areas selected include implementation of: Environmental and social Impact Assessments, biodiversity and ecosystem management, pollution and waste management.",""],[1,"44","2","Biodiversity and Ecosystem Management","High impact areas selected include implementation of: Environmental and social Impact Assessments, biodiversity and ecosystem management, pollution and waste management.",""],[1,"44","2","Pollution and Waste Management","High impact areas selected include implementation of: Environmental and social Impact Assessments, biodiversity and ecosystem management, pollution and waste management.",""],[1,"44","4","Stakeholder Coordination and Engagement Mechanism","Improving coordination and engagement of all stakeholders to enhance information sharing, timely response and joint delivery of interventions;",""]]}});